a:1583:{s:10:"pluginname";s:11:"Boost Union";s:12:"choosereadme";s:394:"Theme Boost Union is an enhanced child theme of Boost which is intended, on the one hand, to make Boost simply more configurable and, on the other hand, to provide helpful additional features for the daily Moodle operation of admins, teachers and students. Boost Union is maintained by Moodle an Hochschulen e.V., in cooperation with ssystems GmbH, together with bdecent GmbH and lern.link GmbH";s:11:"configtitle";s:11:"Boost Union";s:16:"githubissueslink";s:100:"<a href="https://github.com/moodle-an-hochschulen/moodle-theme_boost_union/issues">Github issues</a>";s:25:"warningboostunioninactive";s:286:"Boost Union (or a child theme of Boost Union) is currently <em>not</em> the active theme. Settings on these pages will not have any effect if you do not <a href="{$a->url}">make Boost Union the active theme</a> or allow Boost Union to be used as category / course / user / cohort theme.";s:5:"never";s:5:"Never";s:6:"always";s:6:"Always";s:4:"auto";s:13:"Automatically";s:12:"bycapability";s:24:"Controlled by capability";s:8:"nochange";s:9:"No change";s:13:"forguestsonly";s:39:"Only for guests and non-logged-in users";s:10:"showastext";s:12:"Show as text";s:11:"showasbadge";s:13:"Show as badge";s:27:"imageposition_center_center";s:34:"Center horizontally and vertically";s:24:"imageposition_center_top";s:35:"Center horizontally, top vertically";s:27:"imageposition_center_bottom";s:38:"Center horizontally, bottom vertically";s:22:"imageposition_left_top";s:33:"Left horizontally, top vertically";s:25:"imageposition_left_center";s:36:"Left horizontally, center vertically";s:25:"imageposition_left_bottom";s:36:"Left horizontally, bottom vertically";s:23:"imageposition_right_top";s:34:"Right horizontally, top vertically";s:26:"imageposition_right_center";s:37:"Right horizontally, center vertically";s:26:"imageposition_right_bottom";s:37:"Right horizontally, bottom vertically";s:32:"logininstructionposition_between";s:47:"Between the intro and the login provider widget";s:30:"logininstructionposition_below";s:31:"Below the login provider widget";s:24:"buttoncolorprimaryfilled";s:16:"Primary (Filled)";s:26:"buttoncolorsecondaryfilled";s:18:"Secondary (Filled)";s:25:"buttoncolorprimaryoutline";s:17:"Primary (Outline)";s:27:"buttoncolorsecondaryoutline";s:19:"Secondary (Outline)";s:29:"buttoncolorlightmoodleoutline";s:32:"Moodle Light Secondary (Outline)";s:15:"buttonsizesmall";s:5:"Small";s:16:"buttonsizemedium";s:6:"Medium";s:15:"buttonsizelarge";s:5:"Large";s:15:"bootstrap0to5_0";s:8:"0 (None)";s:15:"bootstrap0to5_1";s:15:"1 (Extra small)";s:15:"bootstrap0to5_2";s:9:"2 (Small)";s:15:"bootstrap0to5_3";s:10:"3 (Medium)";s:15:"bootstrap0to5_4";s:9:"4 (Large)";s:15:"bootstrap0to5_5";s:15:"5 (Extra large)";s:24:"horizontalalignment_left";s:4:"Left";s:26:"horizontalalignment_center";s:8:"Centered";s:25:"horizontalalignment_right";s:5:"Right";s:16:"pagelayout_admin";s:20:"Administration pages";s:15:"pagelayout_base";s:11:"Base layout";s:17:"pagelayout_course";s:17:"Course main pages";s:25:"pagelayout_coursecategory";s:21:"Course category pages";s:20:"pagelayout_frontpage";s:14:"Site home page";s:19:"pagelayout_incourse";s:33:"Course sub pages / Activity pages";s:16:"pagelayout_login";s:10:"Login page";s:20:"pagelayout_mycourses";s:10:"My courses";s:22:"pagelayout_mydashboard";s:9:"Dashboard";s:19:"pagelayout_mypublic";s:13:"User profiles";s:17:"pagelayout_report";s:12:"Report pages";s:19:"pagelayout_standard";s:15:"Standard layout";s:10:"dontchange";s:22:"Do not change anything";s:16:"tertiarysettings";s:34:"List of Boost Union settings pages";s:32:"settingoverridenotificationtitle";s:26:"Possible setting overrides";s:25:"settingoverrideactioninfo";s:34:"Explain setting possible overrides";s:29:"settingoverrideactionflavours";s:15:"Manage flavours";s:24:"settingoverrideactionmwp";s:23:"Manage tenant brandings";s:23:"settingoverridemodallms";s:382:"<strong>Flavours</strong><br />Boost Union's flavours offer a possibility to override particular Moodle look & feel settings in particular contexts. Here, the global default setting is defined. And with flavours, you can differentiate the setting for particular contexts or user groups. Click on the 'Manage flavours' icon to go to the flavours management page and define a flavour.";s:23:"settingoverridemodalmwp";s:404:"<strong>Tenant brandings</strong><br />Boost Union's tenant brandings offer a possibility to override particular Moodle look & feel settings for particular tenants. Here, the global default setting is defined. And with tenant brandings, you can differentiate the setting for particular tenants. Click on the 'Manage tenant brandings' icon to go to the tenant management page and define a tenant branding.";s:26:"settingoverridemodallmsmwp";s:197:"<strong>Order</strong><br />If you have defined both flavours and tenant overrides for a particular Boost Union setting, the flavour override will take precedence over the tenant branding override.";s:18:"settingoverridelms";s:59:"This setting can be overridden within Boost Union flavours.";s:21:"settingoverridelmsmwp";s:84:"This setting can be overridden within the tenant brandings and Boost Union flavours.";s:18:"settingoverridemwp";s:59:"This setting can be overridden within the tenant brandings.";s:20:"settingsupplementlms";s:61:"This setting can be supplemented within Boost Union flavours.";s:23:"settingsupplementlmsmwp";s:86:"This setting can be supplemented within the tenant brandings and Boost Union flavours.";s:20:"settingsupplementmwp";s:61:"This setting can be supplemented within the tenant brandings.";s:16:"settingsoverview";s:17:"Settings overview";s:22:"settingsoverview_title";s:29:"Boost Union settings overview";s:26:"settingsoverview_look_desc";s:115:"Settings for branding your Moodle site are located here: Colors, icons, images, sizing and, of course, custom SCSS.";s:26:"settingsoverview_feel_desc";s:128:"Settings for the overall behaviour of your Moodle site are located here: Navigation items, navigation helpers, blocks and links.";s:29:"settingsoverview_content_desc";s:138:"Settings for the global content of your Moodle site are located here: Footer, static pages, info banners, advertisement tiles and sliders.";s:35:"settingsoverview_functionality_desc";s:107:"Settings for additional useful global or course-related functionality on your Moodle site are located here.";s:35:"settingsoverview_accessibility_desc";s:86:"Settings for accessibility-related functionality on your Moodle site are located here.";s:30:"settingsoverview_flavours_desc";s:105:"With flavours, you can diversify the look of your Moodle site between cohorts and / or course categories.";s:30:"settingsoverview_snippets_desc";s:92:"With SCSS snippets, you can enable additional eye candy or visual fixes on your Moodle site.";s:32:"settingsoverview_smartmenus_desc";s:156:"With smart menus, you can extend the navigation items of your Moodle site in the main menu and the user menus well as introduce a bottom menu or a top menu.";s:37:"settingsoverview_recommendations_desc";s:133:"Recommendations highlight relevant Moodle core, Boost Union and third-party plugin settings to allow a more robust Boost Union setup.";s:20:"settingsoverview_all";s:24:"All settings on one page";s:25:"settingsoverview_all_desc";s:147:"Here, you can open the standard Moodle category settings page for Boost Union that shows all settings on one page. But beware, it is really packed.";s:15:"configtitlelook";s:4:"Look";s:13:"presetheading";s:13:"Theme presets";s:18:"presetheading_desc";s:261:"Theme presets can be used to dramatically alter the appearance of the theme. Boost Union does not re-implement the theme preset setting. If you want to use theme presets, please set them directly in Boost. Boost Union will inherit and use the configured preset.";s:12:"presetbutton";s:25:"Set theme preset in Boost";s:7:"scsstab";s:4:"SCSS";s:11:"scssheading";s:8:"Raw SCSS";s:14:"extscssheading";s:13:"External SCSS";s:19:"extscssheading_desc";s:272:"In addition to the raw SCSS settings above, Boost Union can load SCSS from an external source. It is included before the SCSS code which is defined above which means that you can manage a centralized external SCSS codebase and can still amend it with local SCSS additions.";s:20:"extscssheading_instr";s:13:"Instructions:";s:19:"extscssheading_drop";s:170:"If Boost Union cannot fetch the external SCSS file for any reason, it will simply ignore the external SCSS file to avoid hickups with SCSS compiling and broken frontends.";s:24:"extscssheading_structure";s:116:"The external SCSS must be provided as plaintext file, without any headers or footers, containing just the SCSS code.";s:22:"extscssheading_prepost";s:200:"Just like the raw SCSS settings above, the external SCSS is split into two pieces: Pre and Post SCSS. Pre SCSS can be used for initializing SCSS variables, Post SCSS is used for your actual SCSS code.";s:22:"extscssheading_sources";s:267:"You can configure Boost Union to fetch the external SCSS file either from a public download URL (which will be accessed and fetched with an unauthenticated cURL request) or from a private Github repository (which will be accessed and fetched with a Github API token).";s:19:"extscssheading_task";s:215:"There is a <a href="{$a}">scheduled task theme_boost_union\task\purge_cache</a> which is disabled by default but which you can enable if you want Boost Union to periodically fetch and compile the external SCSS code.";s:10:"invalidurl";s:24:"The given URL is invalid";s:13:"extscsssource";s:20:"External SCSS source";s:18:"extscsssource_desc";s:71:"Pick the type of source from where you want to fetch the external SCSS.";s:17:"extscsssourcenone";s:4:"None";s:21:"extscsssourcedownload";s:19:"Public download URL";s:19:"extscsssourcegithub";s:25:"Private Github repository";s:13:"extscssurlpre";s:30:"External Pre SCSS download URL";s:18:"extscssurlpre_desc";s:75:"The public download URL from where the External Pre SCSS should be fetched.";s:14:"extscssurlpost";s:31:"External Post SCSS download URL";s:19:"extscssurlpost_desc";s:76:"The public download URL from where the external Post SCSS should be fetched.";s:18:"extscssgithubtoken";s:30:"External SCSS Github API token";s:23:"extscssgithubtoken_desc";s:104:"The Github API token which will be used to fetch the SCSS code from the given private Github repository.";s:23:"extscssgithubtoken_docs";s:145:"Go to <a href="https://github.com/settings/tokens">your Github token settings</a> to generate an API token and to see the official documentation.";s:17:"extscssgithubuser";s:29:"External SCSS Github API user";s:22:"extscssgithubuser_desc";s:77:"The Github API user or organization which owns the private Github repository.";s:25:"extscssgithubuser_example";s:209:"Example: If you can see the file in your Github account on https://github.com/moodle-an-hochschulen/moodle-theme_boost_union-extscsstest/blob/main/extscss.scss, the user will be <em>moodle-an-hochschulen</em>.";s:17:"extscssgithubrepo";s:35:"External SCSS Github API repository";s:22:"extscssgithubrepo_desc";s:63:"The private Github repository where the SCSS files are located.";s:25:"extscssgithubrepo_example";s:230:"Example: If you can see the file in your Github account on https://github.com/moodle-an-hochschulen/moodle-theme_boost_union-extscsstest/blob/main/extscss.scss, the repository will be <em>moodle-theme_boost_union-extscsstest</em>.";s:24:"extscssgithubprefilepath";s:34:"External Pre SCSS Github file path";s:29:"extscssgithubprefilepath_desc";s:81:"The path within the private Github repository where the Pre SCSS file is located.";s:29:"extscssgithubfilepath_example";s:206:"Example: If you can see the file in your Github account on https://github.com/moodle-an-hochschulen/moodle-theme_boost_union-extscsstest/blob/main/extscss.scss, the file path will be <em>/extscss.scss</em>.";s:25:"extscssgithubpostfilepath";s:35:"External Post SCSS Github file path";s:30:"extscssgithubpostfilepath_desc";s:82:"The path within the private Github repository where the Post SCSS file is located.";s:24:"extscssvalidationsetting";s:24:"External SCSS validation";s:29:"extscssvalidationsetting_desc";s:586:"If this setting is enabled, the external SCSS is validated if it can be compiled before it is added to the SCSS stack. External SCSS code which can't be compiled is silently ignored and not used. However, this validation is only run on the external SCSS code only, it is not run on the combined SCSS stack which would be the result of the integration of the external SCSS. This means that, as soon as you use SCSS variables from Moodle core or Bootstrap in your external SCSS, you have to disable the validation and verify yourself that the SCSS code is valid to avoid broken frontends.";s:7:"pagetab";s:4:"Page";s:16:"pagewidthheading";s:10:"Page width";s:28:"coursecontentmaxwidthsetting";s:24:"Course content max width";s:33:"coursecontentmaxwidthsetting_desc";s:388:"With this setting, you can override Moodle's course content width without manual SCSS modifications. This width is used as page width of course pages and within several activities. By default, Moodle uses a course content max width of 830px. You can enter other pixel-based values like 1200px, but you can also enter a percentage-based value like 100% or a viewport-width value like 90vw.";s:28:"mediumcontentmaxwidthsetting";s:24:"Medium content max width";s:33:"mediumcontentmaxwidthsetting_desc";s:383:"With this setting, you can override Moodle's medium content width without manual SCSS modifications. This page width is used in certain activities like the database activity. By default, Moodle uses a medium content max width of 1120px. You can enter other pixel-based values like 1200px, but you can also enter a percentage-based value like 100% or a viewport-width value like 90vw.";s:18:"drawerwidthheading";s:12:"Drawer width";s:29:"courseindexdrawerwidthsetting";s:25:"Course index drawer width";s:34:"courseindexdrawerwidthsetting_desc";s:313:"With this setting, you can override Moodle's course index drawer width without manual SCSS modifications. By default, Moodle uses a course index drawer width of 285px. You can enter other pixel-based values like 320px, but values with other units like percentage-based values or a viewport-width value won't work.";s:23:"blockdrawerwidthsetting";s:18:"Block drawer width";s:28:"blockdrawerwidthsetting_desc";s:305:"With this setting, you can override Moodle's block drawer width without manual SCSS modifications. By default, Moodle uses a medium content max width of 315px. You can enter other pixel-based values like 400px, but values with other units like percentage-based values or a viewport-width value won't work.";s:15:"sitebrandingtab";s:13:"Site branding";s:12:"logosheading";s:5:"Logos";s:11:"logosetting";s:4:"Logo";s:16:"logosetting_desc";s:187:"Here, you can upload a full logo to be used as decoration. This image is especially used on the login page. This image can be quite high resolution because it will be scaled down for use.";s:18:"logocompactsetting";s:12:"Compact logo";s:23:"logocompactsetting_desc";s:231:"Here, you can upload a compact version of the same logo as above, such as an emblem, shield or icon. This image is especially used in the navigation bar at the top of each Moodle page. The image should be clear even at small sizes.";s:14:"faviconheading";s:7:"Favicon";s:14:"faviconsetting";s:7:"Favicon";s:19:"faviconsetting_desc";s:197:"Here, you can upload a custom image (.ico or .png format) that the browser will show as the favicon of your Moodle website. If no custom favicon is uploaded, a standard Moodle favicon will be used.";s:23:"backgroundimagesheading";s:25:"General background images";s:22:"backgroundimagesetting";s:16:"Background image";s:27:"backgroundimagesetting_desc";s:175:"Here, you can upload a custom image to display as a background of the site. The background image you upload here will override the background image in your theme preset files.";s:30:"backgroundimagepositionsetting";s:25:"Background image position";s:35:"backgroundimagepositionsetting_desc";s:184:"With this setting, you control the positioning of the background image within the browser window. The first value is the horizontal position, the second value is the vertical position.";s:18:"brandcolorsheading";s:12:"Brand colors";s:10:"brandcolor";s:19:"Primary brand color";s:15:"brandcolor_desc";s:275:"The primary brand color. It is used for accent and highlighting purposes across the site and is also used as basis for calculating gradated brand colors. Furthermore, it is used for links and buttons unless you set distinct colors for links and buttons in the settings below.";s:16:"brandedgraytones";s:22:"Use branded gray tones";s:21:"brandedgraytones_desc";s:300:"With this setting, the Bootstrap gray tones used throughout the theme are derived from the primary brand color instead of neutral grays. This creates a subtle color harmony across all gray elements on the page. Please note: This setting only takes effect if a primary brand color is configured above.";s:17:"linkcolorsheading";s:11:"Link colors";s:16:"linkcolorsetting";s:16:"Link brand color";s:21:"linkcolorsetting_desc";s:134:"With this setting, you can set a dedicated brand color for links. If this setting is empty, Boost Union's primary brand color is used.";s:23:"buttonbrandcolorsetting";s:18:"Button brand color";s:28:"buttonbrandcolorsetting_desc";s:147:"With this setting, you can define a dedicated brand color for primary buttons. If this setting is empty, Boost Union's primary brand color is used.";s:22:"bootstrapcolorsheading";s:16:"Bootstrap colors";s:28:"bootstrapcolorsuccesssetting";s:29:"Bootstrap color for "Success"";s:33:"bootstrapcolorsuccesssetting_desc";s:33:"The Bootstrap color for "Success"";s:25:"bootstrapcolorinfosetting";s:26:"Bootstrap color for "Info"";s:30:"bootstrapcolorinfosetting_desc";s:30:"The Bootstrap color for "Info"";s:28:"bootstrapcolorwarningsetting";s:29:"Bootstrap color for "Warning"";s:33:"bootstrapcolorwarningsetting_desc";s:33:"The Bootstrap color for "Warning"";s:27:"bootstrapcolordangersetting";s:28:"Bootstrap color for "Danger"";s:32:"bootstrapcolordangersetting_desc";s:32:"The Bootstrap color for "Danger"";s:13:"navbarheading";s:6:"Navbar";s:12:"maxlogowidth";s:31:"Maximal width of logo in navbar";s:17:"maxlogowidth_desc";s:463:"In the navbar, the uploaded compact logo is normally displayed with 100% height and proportional width. However, if the logo is too broad or has another special aspect ratio, you can set the maximal width of the logo in the navbar here. You can enter pixel-based values like 120px, but you can also enter a percentage-based value like 10% or a viewport-width value like 5vw. If you do not enter any value, the logo will be displayed with the default presentation.";s:16:"maxsitenamewidth";s:35:"Maximal width of sitename in navbar";s:21:"maxsitenamewidth_desc";s:517:"If you have a very long sitename and want to prevent it from breaking the navbar layout (especially the edit button widget) on medium-width screens, you can set the maximal width of the sitename in the navbar here. If the sitename exceeds this width, it will be truncated with an ellipsis (...). You can enter pixel-based values like 200px, but you can also enter a percentage-based value like 20% or a viewport-width value like 15vw. If you do not enter any value, the sitename will be displayed with its full width.";s:18:"navbarcolorsetting";s:12:"Navbar color";s:23:"navbarcolorsetting_desc";s:112:"With this setting, you can change the navbar color from the default light navbar to a dark one or a colored one.";s:24:"navbarcolorsetting_light";s:73:"Light navbar with dark font color (unchanged as presented by Moodle core)";s:23:"navbarcolorsetting_dark";s:33:"Dark navbar with light font color";s:30:"navbarcolorsetting_coloreddark";s:36:"Colored navbar with light font color";s:31:"navbarcolorsetting_coloredlight";s:35:"Colored navbar with dark font color";s:17:"navbartintsetting";s:11:"Navbar tint";s:22:"navbartintsetting_desc";s:251:"With this setting, you can define the color of the colored navbar. This setting is only effective if the navbar color is set to one of the 'Colored navbar' options above. If no color is defined here, the primary brand color will be used as a fallback.";s:19:"activitybrandingtab";s:17:"Activity branding";s:25:"activityiconcolorsheading";s:20:"Activity icon colors";s:38:"activityiconcoloradministrationsetting";s:40:"Activity icon color for "Administration"";s:43:"activityiconcoloradministrationsetting_desc";s:44:"The activity icon color for "Administration"";s:34:"activityiconcolorassessmentsetting";s:36:"Activity icon color for "Assessment"";s:39:"activityiconcolorassessmentsetting_desc";s:40:"The activity icon color for "Assessment"";s:37:"activityiconcolorcollaborationsetting";s:39:"Activity icon color for "Collaboration"";s:42:"activityiconcolorcollaborationsetting_desc";s:43:"The activity icon color for "Collaboration"";s:37:"activityiconcolorcommunicationsetting";s:39:"Activity icon color for "Communication"";s:42:"activityiconcolorcommunicationsetting_desc";s:43:"The activity icon color for "Communication"";s:31:"activityiconcolorcontentsetting";s:33:"Activity icon color for "Content"";s:36:"activityiconcolorcontentsetting_desc";s:37:"The activity icon color for "Content"";s:42:"activityiconcolorinteractivecontentsetting";s:45:"Activity icon color for "Interactive content"";s:47:"activityiconcolorinteractivecontentsetting_desc";s:49:"The activity icon color for "Interactive content"";s:33:"activityiconcolorinterfacesetting";s:35:"Activity icon color for "Interface"";s:38:"activityiconcolorinterfacesetting_desc";s:39:"The activity icon color for "Interface"";s:32:"activityiconcolorfidelitysetting";s:28:"Activity icon color fidelity";s:37:"activityiconcolorfidelitysetting_desc";s:759:"With the settings above, you set a hex color which will be used to tint the particular activity icon. However, technically, the activity icon is tinted with a CSS filter. Boost Union uses a sophisticated algorithm to determine a CSS filter which matches the given hex color visually, but this algorithm is based on a randomized search and might produce suboptimal results when it is run just once. With this setting, you can allow Boost Union to run the algorithm multiple times and pick the filter which deviates least from the hex color at the end. Please note that this setting has an impact on the cache purging times (the more iterations you allow, the longer Moodle will take to purge the theme cache), but it will not have an impact on page load times.";s:33:"activityiconcolorfidelity_oneshot";s:22:"One shot (1 iteration)";s:35:"activityiconcolorfidelity_sometries";s:32:"Some tries (up to 10 iterations)";s:35:"activityiconcolorfidelity_detailled";s:41:"Detailled research (up to 100 iterations)";s:32:"activityiconcolorfidelity_insane";s:35:"Insane quest (up to 500 iterations)";s:22:"activitypurposeheading";s:22:"Activity icon purposes";s:27:"activitypurposeheading_desc";s:175:"With these settings, you can override the activity icon background color which is defined by the activity's purpose (and which is a hardcoded plugin feature in each activity).";s:30:"activitypurposeheadingtechnote";s:385:"Technical note: Due to the way how Moodle core implements the activity purposes and their colors, the activity purposes are only overridden with CSS by Boost Union. Currently, all areas in Moodle core which show colored activity icons should be covered. If you spot any area or third party plugin which continues to show the unchanged activity purpose colors, please report it on {$a}.";s:29:"activitypurposeadministration";s:14:"Administration";s:25:"activitypurposeassessment";s:10:"Assessment";s:28:"activitypurposecollaboration";s:13:"Collaboration";s:28:"activitypurposecommunication";s:13:"Communication";s:22:"activitypurposecontent";s:7:"Content";s:33:"activitypurposeinteractivecontent";s:19:"Interactive content";s:24:"activitypurposeinterface";s:9:"Interface";s:20:"activitypurposeother";s:5:"Other";s:15:"modiconsheading";s:14:"Activity icons";s:21:"modiconsenablesetting";s:48:"Enable custom icons for activities and resources";s:26:"modiconsenablesetting_desc";s:146:"With this setting, you can modify the icons for activities and resources which are used by Moodle on the course pages and in the activity chooser.";s:13:"modiconsfiles";s:18:"Custom icons files";s:18:"modiconsfiles_desc";s:106:"Here, you can upload custom icons for all or only some activity modules installed in this Moodle instance.";s:18:"modiconsfileshowto";s:754:"To upload a particular custom activity icon, start by creating a folder with the internal name of the activity, e.g. <em>assign</em> for the assigment activity. In this folder, you upload the icon as SVG file called monologo.svg and, if possible, as fallback PNG file called monologo.png. If you want to customize the colored icons which have been in use up to Moodle 3 and which may still be used by older plugins, you can also upload them as icon.svg and icon.png files. However, please stick to monochromatic SVG icons if possible for best results. Then, please save the settings page. As soon as you have save the setting with at least one file, a file list will appear below which helps you to check if the custom icons have been uploaded correctly.";s:17:"modiconsfilestech";s:324:"Technical note: After saving the setting, the uploaded folder structure and icon files will be copied to the pix_plugins/mod folder in your Moodledata directory. This is where Moodle core searches for custom activity icons. All icon files which may already exist in this place will be overwritten when you save this setting.";s:18:"modiconlistsetting";s:23:"Custom icons files list";s:23:"modiconlistsetting_desc";s:270:"This is the list of custom icon files which you have uploaded to the custom icon files filearea above. All valid icon files are listed here. In addition to that, other files you may have uploaded as well but which are not valid icon files are also shown as broken files.";s:16:"modiconsuccess4x";s:71:"This icon will be used for the <em>{$a}</em> activity as Moodle 4 icon.";s:16:"modiconsuccess3x";s:78:"This icon will be used for the <em>{$a}</em> activity as Moodle 3 legacy icon.";s:15:"modiconnamefail";s:286:"This file was uploaded into the correct folder for the <em>{$a}</em> activity, but the filename is not valid. Please change the filename to either <em>monologo.svg</em> / <em>monologo.png</em> (for Moodle 4 icons) or to <em>icon.svg</em> / <em>icon.png</em> (for Moodle 3 legacy icons).";s:15:"modiconnotexist";s:133:"This file was upload to an unsuitable location as it’s impossible to deduce a particular activity from the file path <em>{$a}</em>.";s:15:"modiconactivity";s:8:"Activity";s:22:"modiconactivityunknown";s:7:"Unknown";s:14:"modiconversion";s:12:"Icon version";s:16:"modicongtmoodle4";s:13:"Moodle 4 icon";s:18:"modiconltmoodle311";s:20:"Moodle 3 legacy icon";s:19:"calendarbrandingtab";s:17:"Calendar branding";s:25:"calendareventtypecategory";s:8:"Category";s:23:"calendareventtypecourse";s:6:"Course";s:22:"calendareventtypegroup";s:5:"Group";s:22:"calendareventtypeother";s:5:"Other";s:21:"calendareventtypesite";s:4:"Site";s:21:"calendareventtypeuser";s:4:"User";s:26:"calendareventcolorsheading";s:25:"Calendar event type: {$a}";s:29:"calendareventcolormainsetting";s:44:"Main color of the calendar event type "{$a}"";s:34:"calendareventcolormainsetting_desc";s:89:"The main color of the calendar event type "{$a}" which is used for icons and backgrounds.";s:31:"calendareventcolorbordersetting";s:46:"Border color of the calendar event type "{$a}"";s:36:"calendareventcolorbordersetting_desc";s:70:"The color of the calendar event type "{$a}" which is used for borders.";s:23:"calendarbrandingheading";s:25:"General calendar branding";s:25:"calendariconscolorsetting";s:20:"Calendar icon colors";s:30:"calendariconscolorsetting_desc";s:170:"The color of some icons which are used in the calendar views. The default color is blue, but this might clash with the calendar branding colors which you might set above.";s:12:"loginpagetab";s:10:"Login page";s:23:"loginarrangementheading";s:22:"Login page arrangement";s:24:"loginformpositionsetting";s:24:"Login container position";s:29:"loginformpositionsetting_desc";s:402:"With this setting, you can optimize the login container to fit to a greater variety of background images. By default, the login container is displayed centered on the login page. Alternatively, you can move it to the left or to the right of the login page to let other parts of the background image shine through. Of course, you can also change this setting if no background images are uploaded at all.";s:31:"loginformpositionsetting_center";s:8:"Centered";s:29:"loginformpositionsetting_left";s:12:"Left-aligned";s:30:"loginformpositionsetting_right";s:13:"Right-aligned";s:33:"loginformpositionsetting_semileft";s:17:"Semi-left-aligned";s:34:"loginformpositionsetting_semiright";s:18:"Semi-right-aligned";s:28:"loginformtransparencysetting";s:28:"Login container transparency";s:33:"loginformtransparencysetting_desc";s:125:"With this setting, you can make the login container slightly transparent to let the background image shine through even more.";s:26:"logincontainerwidthsetting";s:21:"Login container width";s:31:"logincontainerwidthsetting_desc";s:314:"With this setting, you can override Moodle's fixed login container width of 500px. By default, Moodle uses a login container width of 500px on medium and larger screens. You can enter other pixel-based values like 600px, but you can also enter a percentage-based value like 90% or a viewport-width value like 50vw.";s:31:"logincontainerwidthsetting_note";s:308:"Please note: If you use the tabs login form layout, the login container might become wider than the defined width if you have many login providers enabled or if you have long login tab texts. In this case, the login container will try to expand horizontally to fit all login provider tabs next to each other.";s:28:"loginbackgroundimagesheading";s:28:"Login page background images";s:20:"loginbackgroundimage";s:28:"Login page background images";s:25:"loginbackgroundimage_desc";s:269:"The images to display as a background of the login page. One of these images will be picked randomly and shown when the user visits the login page. Please make sure not to use non-ASCII-characters in the filename if you want to display text for login background images.";s:35:"loginbackgroundimagepositionsetting";s:36:"Login page background image position";s:40:"loginbackgroundimagepositionsetting_desc";s:195:"With this setting, you control the positioning of the login page background image within the browser window. The first value is the horizontal position, the second value is the vertical position.";s:31:"loginbackgroundimagetextsetting";s:40:"Display text for login background images";s:36:"loginbackgroundimagetextsetting_desc";s:794:"With this optional setting you can add text, e.g. a copyright notice to your uploaded background images. This text will appear on top of the page footer on the login page. However, for screen real estate reasons, it is only shown on larger screen sizes.<br/>
Each line consists of the file identifier (the file name), the text that should be displayed and the text color, separated by a pipe character. Each declaration needs to be written in a new line. <br/>
For example:<br/>
background-image-1.jpg|Copyright: CC0|dark<br/>
As text color, you can use the values "dark" or "light".<br />
You can declare texts for an arbitrary amount of your uploaded login background images. The texts will be added only to those images that match their filename with the identifier declared in this setting.";s:20:"loginbrandingheading";s:19:"Login page branding";s:17:"loginpagebranding";s:16:"Login page brand";s:22:"loginpagebranding_desc";s:196:"With this setting, you can control which branding elements are shown on the login page. Depending on your choice, the logo (if uploaded), the site heading, and/or a site tagline will be displayed.";s:33:"loginpagebrand_logoheadingtagline";s:38:"Logo (if uploaded) + heading + tagline";s:35:"loginpagebrand_logootherwiseheading";s:75:"Logo (if uploaded), heading otherwise (Unchanged as handled by Moodle core)";s:26:"loginpagebrand_logoheading";s:28:"Logo (if uploaded) + heading";s:26:"loginpagebrand_logotagline";s:28:"Logo (if uploaded) + tagline";s:29:"loginpagebrand_headingtagline";s:17:"Heading + tagline";s:22:"loginpagebrand_heading";s:7:"Heading";s:22:"loginpagebrand_tagline";s:7:"Tagline";s:23:"loginpageheadingsetting";s:18:"Login page heading";s:28:"loginpageheadingsetting_desc";s:91:"With this setting, you can control what text is displayed as the heading on the login page.";s:31:"loginpageheadingsetting_options";s:299:"On the one hand, you can choose between multiple variations of the presentation of the site name. On the other hand, you can choose a simple greeting message. The 'Welcome! / Welcome back!' option tries to detect if the user is a returning visitor and will present the matching greeting accordingly.";s:23:"loginpagetaglinesetting";s:18:"Login page tagline";s:28:"loginpagetaglinesetting_desc";s:91:"With this setting, you can control what text is displayed as the tagline on the login page.";s:22:"loginpagelabel_welcome";s:8:"Welcome!";s:26:"loginpagelabel_welcomeback";s:13:"Welcome back!";s:24:"loginpagelabel_welcometo";s:15:"Welcome to {$a}";s:24:"loginlogomaxwidthsetting";s:20:"Login logo max width";s:29:"loginlogomaxwidthsetting_desc";s:258:"With this setting, you can restrict the maximum width of the logo on the login page. You can enter pixel-based values like 120px, but you can also enter a percentage-based value like 10%. If you do not enter any value, the logo will be scaled proportionally.";s:25:"loginlogomaxheightsetting";s:21:"Login logo max height";s:30:"loginlogomaxheightsetting_desc";s:259:"With this setting, you can restrict the maximum height of the logo on the login page. You can enter pixel-based values like 120px, but you can also enter a percentage-based value like 10%. If you do not enter any value, the logo will be scaled proportionally.";s:25:"loginlogoalignmentsetting";s:20:"Login logo alignment";s:30:"loginlogoalignmentsetting_desc";s:90:"With this setting, you can control the horizontal alignment of the logo on the login page.";s:28:"loginlogomarginbottomsetting";s:24:"Login logo margin bottom";s:33:"loginlogomarginbottomsetting_desc";s:229:"With this setting, you can control the bottom margin of the logo on the login page by adding a Bootstrap spacing class (mb-0 to mb-5) to the logo container. This will help you to optimize the vertical whitespace around your logo.";s:18:"loginlayoutheading";s:17:"Login form layout";s:18:"loginlayoutsetting";s:17:"Login form layout";s:23:"loginlayoutsetting_desc";s:397:"With this setting, you control how the login providers are displayed on the login page. You can choose between a vertical layout (all login providers displayed one below the other), a tabbed layout (login providers displayed in tabs next to each other), or an accordion layout (login providers displayed one below the other, but collapsed by default and expandable by clicking on the intro texts).";s:19:"loginlayoutvertical";s:30:"Vertical (one below the other)";s:15:"loginlayouttabs";s:25:"Tabs (next to each other)";s:20:"loginlayoutaccordion";s:33:"Accordion (collapsed, expandable)";s:30:"loginenhancedtabslayoutsetting";s:30:"Enhanced tabs layout behaviour";s:35:"loginenhancedtabslayoutsetting_desc";s:818:"The tabs layout generally respects the configured login container width, as described in the login container width setting. And the login container of the tabs layout is displayed vertically centered just like the other login form layouts. However, there might be configurations when this is not enough. Maybe the height of the particular tab panes differ too much so that the tabs jump vertically when the active tab is changed. Or maybe really long tab labels widen the login container width, but multiline login instruction texts do not adapt accordingly. These are edge cases which cannot be solved cleanly with CSS and for such cases, you can add a JavaScript module which, after the login page has loaded, tries to ensure that all the login content is still presented and positioned as appropriately as possible.";s:24:"logininstructionsheading";s:18:"Login instructions";s:22:"logininstructionsabove";s:38:"Instructions above login provider list";s:27:"logininstructionsabove_desc";s:198:"With this setting, you can add instructions that will be shown above the list of login providers on the login page. This is a good place to add general information that applies to all login methods.";s:22:"logininstructionsbelow";s:38:"Instructions below login provider list";s:27:"logininstructionsbelow_desc";s:219:"With this setting, you can add instructions that will be shown below the list of login providers on the login page. This is a good place to add additional information or support contacts that apply to all login methods.";s:17:"loginorderheading";s:11:"Login order";s:22:"loginorderheading_desc";s:247:"With these settings, you control the order of the login providers in the login form. The presented order will be defined from lowest to highest ordinal number, skipping all login providers and login form elements which are disabled in Boost Union.";s:22:"loginorderlocalsetting";s:11:"Local login";s:20:"loginorderidpsetting";s:9:"IDP login";s:32:"loginorderfirsttimesignupsetting";s:17:"Self registration";s:22:"loginorderguestsetting";s:11:"Guest login";s:19:"primaryloginsetting";s:22:"Primary login provider";s:24:"primaryloginsetting_desc";s:372:"With this setting, you can specify which login provider should be opened by default when the page loads. This setting only applies to the tabs layout and accordion layout. If set to "None", for the tabs layout the first login provider (based on the login order settings) will be opened by default. And for the accordion layout, no login provider will be opened by default.";s:25:"loginproviderlocalheading";s:21:"Login provider: Local";s:28:"loginlocalloginenablesetting";s:11:"Local login";s:33:"loginlocalloginenablesetting_desc";s:348:"With this setting, you control if the local login provider is shown on the login page or not. By default, the local login provider is shown and users can login into the site as normal. If you disable this setting, the local login provider is hidden. This allows you to just provide login buttons for external identity providers like OAuth2 or OIDC.";s:33:"loginlocalloginenablesetting_core";s:256:"Moodle core setting interplay: Boost Union does not process the '{$a->settingname}' setting from <a href="{$a->url}">Moodle core's authentication setting</a>. This setting here is the only place to disable or enable the local login provider in Boost Union.";s:33:"loginlocalloginenablesetting_note";s:484:"Please note: As soon as you hide the local login provider, you risk that admins cannot log in anymore with a local account if there is a problem with the external identity provider. The same goes if no other authentication methods than manual authentication are enabled at all.<br />To allow local logins anyway in such cases, the <a href="{$a->url}">side entrance local login page</a> (see below for details) is enabled automatically. Please bookmark this URL as your own safety net.";s:23:"loginlocalloginformhead";s:11:"Local login";s:31:"loginlocalloginlocalnotdisabled";s:140:"There is no need to log in on this side entrance login page here. Please use the <a href="{$a->url}">standard login page</a> for logging in.";s:26:"loginlocalshowintrosetting";s:17:"Local login intro";s:31:"loginlocalshowintrosetting_desc";s:346:"With this setting, you control if an intro is shown above the local login form or not. By default, the intro is not shown. But if you enable it, this intro may help users to understand which credentials to use in the local login form, especially if you provide more than one login provider or if you have changed the order of the login providers.";s:15:"loginlocalintro";s:30:"Login with your Moodle account";s:26:"loginlocalintrotextsetting";s:22:"Local login intro text";s:31:"loginlocalintrotextsetting_desc";s:142:"With this setting, you can override the default intro text <em>'{$a}'</em> with a custom text. Leave this field empty to use the default text.";s:27:"loginlocalloginlabelsetting";s:17:"Local login label";s:32:"loginlocalloginlabelsetting_desc";s:106:"With this setting, you can customize the label for local login to be used in the tab and accordion layout.";s:35:"loginlocalloginlabelsetting_default";s:14:"Moodle account";s:25:"loginlocalshowinstruction";s:23:"Local login instruction";s:30:"loginlocalshowinstruction_desc";s:76:"With this setting, you can enable instructions for the local login provider.";s:28:"loginlocalinstructioncontent";s:31:"Local login instruction content";s:33:"loginlocalinstructioncontent_desc";s:174:"With this setting, you can specify custom instructions for the local login provider. This allows you to provide users with additional information about how to log in locally.";s:29:"loginlocalinstructionposition";s:32:"Local login instruction position";s:34:"loginlocalinstructionposition_desc";s:113:"With this setting, you can specify where the local login instructions should be shown relative to the login form.";s:28:"loginlocalbuttoncolorsetting";s:24:"Local login button color";s:33:"loginlocalbuttoncolorsetting_desc";s:87:"With this setting, you can control the Bootstrap color style of the local login button.";s:27:"loginlocalbuttonsizesetting";s:23:"Local login button size";s:32:"loginlocalbuttonsizesetting_desc";s:80:"With this setting, you can control the Bootstrap size of the local login button.";s:23:"loginprovideridpheading";s:19:"Login provider: IDP";s:26:"loginidploginenablesetting";s:9:"IDP login";s:31:"loginidploginenablesetting_desc";s:307:"With this setting, you control if the identity provider (IDP) login buttons are shown on the login page or not. By default, IDP login buttons are shown if identity providers are configured. If you disable this setting, all IDP login buttons are hidden regardless of the authentication plugins configuration.";s:31:"loginidploginenablesetting_core";s:242:"Moodle core setting interplay: Identity provider login buttons are provided by authentication plugins like OAuth2, CAS or Shibboleth. You can manage authentication plugins on <a href="{$a->url}">Moodle core's authentication settings page</a>.";s:24:"loginidpshowintrosetting";s:15:"IDP login intro";s:29:"loginidpshowintrosetting_desc";s:360:"With this setting, you control if an intro is shown above the IDP login buttons or not. By default, the intro is shown and users will be quickly informed what the IDP buttons are about. If you disable this setting, the IDP intro is hidden. This allows you to provide a clean user login interface if you just use external identity providers like OAuth2 or OIDC.";s:24:"loginidpintrotextsetting";s:20:"IDP login intro text";s:29:"loginidpintrotextsetting_desc";s:191:"With this setting, you can override the default intro text <em>'{$a}'</em> (which comes from the Moodle core language pack) with a custom text. Leave this field empty to use the default text.";s:25:"loginidploginlabelsetting";s:15:"IDP login label";s:30:"loginidploginlabelsetting_desc";s:104:"With this setting, you can customize the label for IDP login to be used in the tab and accordion layout.";s:33:"loginidploginlabelsetting_default";s:9:"IDP login";s:23:"loginidpshowinstruction";s:21:"IDP login instruction";s:28:"loginidpshowinstruction_desc";s:74:"With this setting, you can enable instructions for the IDP login provider.";s:26:"loginidpinstructioncontent";s:29:"IDP login instruction content";s:31:"loginidpinstructioncontent_desc";s:187:"With this setting, you can specify custom instructions for the IDP login provider. This allows you to provide users with additional information about how to log in via identity providers.";s:27:"loginidpinstructionposition";s:30:"IDP login instruction position";s:32:"loginidpinstructionposition_desc";s:114:"With this setting, you can specify where the IDP login instructions should be shown relative to the login buttons.";s:26:"loginidpbuttoncolorsetting";s:22:"IDP login button color";s:31:"loginidpbuttoncolorsetting_desc";s:86:"With this setting, you can control the Bootstrap color style of the IDP login buttons.";s:25:"loginidpbuttonsizesetting";s:21:"IDP login button size";s:30:"loginidpbuttonsizesetting_desc";s:79:"With this setting, you can control the Bootstrap size of the IDP login buttons.";s:29:"loginprovideridpexpertheading";s:37:"Login provider: IDP (Expert settings)";s:20:"loginidpsplitsetting";s:27:"Split per identity provider";s:25:"loginidpsplitsetting_desc";s:338:"If enabled, each identity provider login option appears in its own tab, accordion panel or section. In tab and accordion layouts, the provider name is used as the label. The IDP intro text and visibility settings still apply within each panel or block. If disabled, all identity providers stay in a single tab, panel, or vertical section.";s:34:"loginshibbolethinternalwayfsetting";s:28:"Use internal Shibboleth WAYF";s:39:"loginshibbolethinternalwayfsetting_desc";s:1392:"With this setting, you can replace a Shibboleth login button with an internal WAYF (Where Are You From) form. This allows you to provide a seamless login experience for Shibboleth users without forcing them to leave the login page.<br />If set to "Yes (based on the 'auth_shibboleth' configuration)", the Shibboleth login button is replaced by the same organisation (IdP) selector as used on the <a href="{$a->loginurl}">Shibboleth authentication plugin's internal login page</a>. The list of organisations comes from the <a href="{$a->settingsurl}">Shibboleth authentication plugin's 'Identity providers' configuration</a>. If that list is empty or Shibboleth authentication is not enabled at all, this setting does not have any effect and IDP buttons are shown as normal.<br />If set to "Yes (based on embedded JavaScript code)", the WAYF code can be configured manually in the 'Embedded WAYF JavaScript code' setting. See the description of that setting for details. Please note that the embedded JavaScript code needs to be able to trigger the login process on the login page by redirecting the user to the correct URL with the correct parameters when an IdP is selected. This setting is especially targetted at Moodle instances which are connected to <a href="https://help.switch.ch/aai/guides/discovery/embedded-wayf/">SWITCH AAI</a> where such a JavaScript code is officially provided.";s:40:"loginshibbolethinternalwayfsettingconfig";s:50:"Yes (based on the 'auth_shibboleth' configuration)";s:38:"loginshibbolethinternalwayfsettingcode";s:39:"Yes (based on embedded JavaScript code)";s:33:"internalshibbolethwayfcodesetting";s:29:"Internal WAYF JavaScript code";s:38:"internalshibbolethwayfcodesetting_desc";s:572:"With this setting, you can embed custom JavaScript code which renders a WAYF element directly on the login page independent from the configuration of 'auth_shibboleth'. Please note that you need to provide the complete JavaScript code including the necessary HTML elements and event handlers for the WAYF functionality. The code will be cleaned to remove malicious code during output, but apart from that it will be output as is. This setting only takes effect if the "Yes (based on JavaScript code)" option is selected in the "Use internal Shibboleth WAYF" setting above.";s:43:"internalshibbolethwayfcodesetting_providers";s:430:"This setting is especially targetted at Moodle instances which are connected to <a href="https://help.switch.ch/aai/guides/discovery/embedded-wayf/">SWITCH AAI</a> where such <a href="https://rr.aai.switch.ch/gen_embedding_code.php">JavaScript code is officially provided</a>. However, you can also use this setting to embed custom JavaScript code for other identity providers if you like to craft your own internal WAYF solution.";s:36:"loginproviderselfregistrationheading";s:33:"Login provider: Self registration";s:34:"loginselfregistrationenablesetting";s:17:"Self registration";s:39:"loginselfregistrationenablesetting_desc";s:288:"With this setting, you control if the self registration button and signup link are shown on the login page or not. By default, self registration is shown if it is enabled in Moodle core. If you disable this setting, self registration is hidden regardless of the core registration setting.";s:39:"loginselfregistrationenablesetting_core";s:189:"Moodle core setting interplay: Self registration is controlled by the '{$a->settingname}' setting which you can manage on <a href="{$a->url}">Moodle core's authentication settings page</a>.";s:37:"loginselfregistrationshowintrosetting";s:23:"Self registration intro";s:42:"loginselfregistrationshowintrosetting_desc";s:257:"With this setting, you control if an intro is shown above the self registration section or not. By default, the intro is shown and helps users to understand what self registration is about. If you disable this setting, the self registration intro is hidden.";s:37:"loginselfregistrationintrotextsetting";s:28:"Self registration intro text";s:42:"loginselfregistrationintrotextsetting_desc";s:191:"With this setting, you can override the default intro text <em>'{$a}'</em> (which comes from the Moodle core language pack) with a custom text. Leave this field empty to use the default text.";s:38:"loginselfregistrationloginlabelsetting";s:23:"Self registration label";s:43:"loginselfregistrationloginlabelsetting_desc";s:112:"With this setting, you can customize the label for self registration to be used in the tab and accordion layout.";s:46:"loginselfregistrationloginlabelsetting_default";s:17:"Self registration";s:36:"loginselfregistrationshowinstruction";s:29:"Self registration instruction";s:41:"loginselfregistrationshowinstruction_desc";s:82:"With this setting, you can enable instructions for the self registration provider.";s:39:"loginselfregistrationinstructioncontent";s:37:"Self registration instruction content";s:44:"loginselfregistrationinstructioncontent_desc";s:186:"With this setting, you can specify custom instructions for the self registration provider. This allows you to provide users with additional information about how to create a new account.";s:40:"loginselfregistrationinstructionposition";s:38:"Self registration instruction position";s:45:"loginselfregistrationinstructionposition_desc";s:121:"With this setting, you can specify where the self registration instruction should be shown relative to the signup button.";s:39:"loginselfregistrationbuttoncolorsetting";s:30:"Self registration button color";s:44:"loginselfregistrationbuttoncolorsetting_desc";s:93:"With this setting, you can control the Bootstrap color style of the self registration button.";s:38:"loginselfregistrationbuttonsizesetting";s:29:"Self registration button size";s:43:"loginselfregistrationbuttonsizesetting_desc";s:86:"With this setting, you can control the Bootstrap size of the self registration button.";s:25:"loginproviderguestheading";s:21:"Login provider: Guest";s:28:"loginguestloginenablesetting";s:11:"Guest login";s:33:"loginguestloginenablesetting_desc";s:285:"With this setting, you control if the guest login button is shown on the login page or not. By default, the guest login button is shown if guest access is enabled in Moodle core. If you disable this setting, the guest login button is hidden regardless of the core guest access setting.";s:33:"loginguestloginenablesetting_core";s:184:"Moodle core setting interplay: Guest access is controlled by the '{$a->settingname}' setting which you can manage on <a href="{$a->url}">Moodle core's authentication settings page</a>.";s:26:"loginguestshowintrosetting";s:17:"Guest login intro";s:31:"loginguestshowintrosetting_desc";s:239:"With this setting, you control if an intro is shown above the guest login button or not. By default, the intro is shown and helps users to understand what guest access is about. If you disable this setting, the guest login intro is hidden.";s:26:"loginguestintrotextsetting";s:22:"Guest login intro text";s:31:"loginguestintrotextsetting_desc";s:191:"With this setting, you can override the default intro text <em>'{$a}'</em> (which comes from the Moodle core language pack) with a custom text. Leave this field empty to use the default text.";s:27:"loginguestloginlabelsetting";s:17:"Guest login label";s:32:"loginguestloginlabelsetting_desc";s:106:"With this setting, you can customize the label for guest login to be used in the tab and accordion layout.";s:35:"loginguestloginlabelsetting_default";s:11:"Guest login";s:25:"loginguestshowinstruction";s:23:"Guest login instruction";s:30:"loginguestshowinstruction_desc";s:76:"With this setting, you can enable instructions for the guest login provider.";s:28:"loginguestinstructioncontent";s:31:"Guest login instruction content";s:33:"loginguestinstructioncontent_desc";s:165:"With this setting, you can specify custom instructions for the guest login provider. This allows you to provide users with additional information about guest access.";s:29:"loginguestinstructionposition";s:32:"Guest login instruction position";s:34:"loginguestinstructionposition_desc";s:114:"With this setting, you can specify where the guest login instruction should be shown relative to the login button.";s:28:"loginguestbuttoncolorsetting";s:24:"Guest login button color";s:33:"loginguestbuttoncolorsetting_desc";s:87:"With this setting, you can control the Bootstrap color style of the guest login button.";s:27:"loginguestbuttonsizesetting";s:23:"Guest login button size";s:32:"loginguestbuttonsizesetting_desc";s:80:"With this setting, you can control the Bootstrap size of the guest login button.";s:24:"sideentranceloginheading";s:19:"Side entrance login";s:30:"sideentranceloginenablesetting";s:26:"Enable side entrance login";s:35:"sideentranceloginenablesetting_desc";s:425:"With this setting, you can enable a <a href="{$a->url}">side entrance local login page</a>. It is enabled automatically if you disable the local login form (see above), but you can also enable it constantly to allow local users to bypass the main login page and login process which is particularly helpful in SSO setups. On the side entrance local login page, all of Moodle's login security measures apply as well, of course.";s:12:"dashboardtab";s:22:"Dashboard / My courses";s:21:"courseoverviewheading";s:21:"Course overview block";s:37:"courseoverviewshowcourseimagessetting";s:18:"Show course images";s:42:"courseoverviewshowcourseimagessetting_desc";s:200:"With this setting, you can control whether the course image is visible inside the course overview block or not. It is possible to choose a different setting for Card view, Summary view, and List view.";s:33:"courseoverviewshowprogresssetting";s:31:"Show course completion progress";s:38:"courseoverviewshowprogresssetting_desc";s:125:"With this setting, you can control whether the course completion progress is visible inside the course overview block or not.";s:26:"courseoverviewimageheading";s:22:"Course overview images";s:32:"courseoverviewimagesourcesetting";s:28:"Course overview image source";s:37:"courseoverviewimagesourcesetting_desc";s:584:"With this setting, you control the source of the image which is shown in the course overview block, on the category index pages and on the course list on site home. The main source for this image is the course image which is uploaded in the particular course's settings. If this image is not available, you can choose if you want to show a generated geometric pattern or a fallback course overview image.<br />Please note: If you use the geometric pattern, you can customize the pattern colors on the <a href="/admin/settings.php?section=coursecolors">course colors settings page</a>.";s:43:"courseoverviewimagesource_coursepluspattern";s:91:"Course image with a fallback to a geometric pattern (unchanged as presented by Moodle core)";s:44:"courseoverviewimagesource_courseplusfallback";s:66:"Course image with a fallback to the course overview fallback image";s:27:"courseoverviewimagefallback";s:30:"Course overview fallback image";s:32:"courseoverviewimagefallback_desc";s:374:"The image which you upload here will be used as a fallback course overview image as soon as the 'Course overview image source' setting is configured likewise.<br />Please note: If you configure the 'Course overview image source' setting to use the course overview fallback image, but you do not upload any image here, the geometric pattern will be used as a fallback anyway.";s:16:"categoryindextab";s:26:"Category index / Site home";s:20:"courselistingheading";s:14:"Course listing";s:25:"courselistingpresentation";s:27:"Course listing presentation";s:30:"courselistingpresentation_desc";s:356:"With this setting, you can modify the look & feel of the course listing on the category index pages and on site home. As an alternative to the way how Moodle core presents them, you can present the course listing as course cards (similar to the course cards on the 'My courses' page) or as course list (similar to the course list on the 'My courses' page).";s:34:"courselistingpresentation_nochange";s:60:"Designer's nightmare (unchanged as presented by Moodle core)";s:31:"courselistingpresentation_cards";s:12:"Course cards";s:30:"courselistingpresentation_list";s:11:"Course list";s:30:"courselistingpresentation_note";s:470:"Please note: If you enable course cards or course lists, the <a href="{$a->url1}">coursesperpage</a> setting is still respected and will control how many cards / rows will be shown. However, the <a href="{$a->url2}">courseswithsummarieslimit</a> setting does not have any effect anymore – all courses will be shown with full details. Please take care not to set <a href="{$a->url1}">coursesperpage</a> too high to avoid long page load times on pages with many courses.";s:22:"coursecardscolumncount";s:24:"Course card column count";s:27:"coursecardscolumncount_desc";s:471:"The course card grid will be presented in a responsive way and its columns will wrap on smaller screens. With this setting, you just control the maximum number of columns in the course card grid on larger screens. Setting the maximum number of columns to 2 instead of 3 might make the course cards look more spacious and less crowded. Setting the maximum number of columns to 1 is possible as well and will effectively turn the course listing in a vertical list of cards.";s:21:"courselistinghowimage";s:39:"Show course image in the course listing";s:26:"courselistinghowimage_desc";s:89:"With this setting, you control if the course image is shown in the course listing or not.";s:25:"courselistingshowcontacts";s:42:"Show course contacts in the course listing";s:30:"courselistingshowcontacts_desc";s:264:"With this setting, you control if the course contact's pictures are shown in the course listing or not. Please note: The contact pictures are shown together with the course image, thus presenting course contacts without presenting the course image is not possible.";s:25:"courselistinghowshortname";s:43:"Show course shortname in the course listing";s:30:"courselistinghowshortname_desc";s:93:"With this setting, you control if the course shortname is shown in the course listing or not.";s:24:"courselistinghowcategory";s:42:"Show course category in the course listing";s:29:"courselistinghowcategory_desc";s:92:"With this setting, you control if the course category is shown in the course listing or not.";s:24:"courselistinghowprogress";s:53:"Show course completion progress in the course listing";s:29:"courselistinghowprogress_desc";s:104:"With this setting, you control if the course completion progress are shown in the course listing or not.";s:25:"courseistingprogressstyle";s:32:"Course completion progress style";s:30:"courseistingprogressstyle_desc";s:146:"With this setting, you control how the course completion progress is displayed. You can choose between a simple percentage text or a progress bar.";s:36:"courseistingprogressstyle_percentage";s:15:"Percentage text";s:29:"courseistingprogressstyle_bar";s:12:"Progress bar";s:26:"courselistinghowenrolicons";s:49:"Show course enrolment icons in the course listing";s:31:"courselistinghowenrolicons_desc";s:100:"With this setting, you control if the course enrolment icons are shown in the course listing or not.";s:23:"courselistingshowfields";s:40:"Show course fields in the course listing";s:28:"courselistingshowfields_desc";s:98:"With this setting, you control if the custom course fields are shown in the course listing or not.";s:25:"courselistingselectfields";s:54:"Select course fields to be shown in the course listing";s:30:"courselistingselectfields_desc";s:149:"With this setting, you can select which specific custom course fields are shown in the course listing. If none are selected, no fields will be shown.";s:33:"courselistingselectfields_nofield";s:244:"With this setting, you can select which specific custom course fields are shown in the course listing. There isn't any usable custom course field yet. Please go the <a href="{$a->url}">{$a->linktitle}</a> and create a custom course field first.";s:24:"courselistingstylefields";s:41:"Style course fields in the course listing";s:29:"courselistingstylefields_desc";s:252:"With this setting, you can control how the custom course fields are displayed in the course listing. You can choose between showing them as text (showing the field value together with the field name as label) or as badge (showing just the field value).";s:20:"courselistinghowgoto";s:38:"Show goto button in the course listing";s:25:"courselistinghowgoto_desc";s:217:"With this setting, you control if a 'Go to course' button is shown in the course listing or not. If this setting is disabled, the user is still able to go to the course by clicking on the course title or course image.";s:17:"courselistinggoto";s:12:"Go to course";s:21:"courselistinghowpopup";s:40:"Show details popup in the course listing";s:26:"courselistinghowpopup_desc";s:337:"With this setting, you control if a 'Course details' button is shown in the course listing or not. With this button, the user can open a details popup which contains the course summary, the course contacts and the course fields. The popup will contain this information regardless if you enabled it on the course card / row itself or not.";s:18:"courselistingpopup";s:7:"Details";s:19:"courselistingummary";s:14:"Course summary";s:22:"courselistingnosummary";s:35:"This course does not have a summary";s:21:"courselistingcontacts";s:14:"Course contact";s:24:"courselistingviewprofile";s:12:"View profile";s:19:"courselistingfields";s:21:"Course classification";s:22:"categorylistingheading";s:16:"Category listing";s:27:"categorylistingpresentation";s:29:"Category listing presentation";s:32:"categorylistingpresentation_desc";s:246:"With this setting, you can modify the look & feel of the category listing on the category index pages and on site home. As an alternative to the way how Moodle core presents them, you can present the category listing as a refreshed list of boxes.";s:36:"categorylistingpresentation_nochange";s:60:"Designer's nightmare (unchanged as presented by Moodle core)";s:35:"categorylistingpresentation_boxlist";s:13:"List of boxes";s:32:"categorylistingpresentation_note";s:158:"Please note: If you enabled the 'Course listing presentation' setting above, we recommend to enable this setting as well. Both were designed to work together.";s:15:"timelineheading";s:14:"Timeline block";s:19:"timelinetintenabled";s:28:"Tint timeline activity icons";s:24:"timelinetintenabled_desc";s:163:"With this setting, you can tint the activity icons in the timeline block based on the activity purposes. By default, Moodle core displays them just as black icons.";s:21:"upcomingeventsheading";s:21:"Upcoming events block";s:25:"upcomingeventstintenabled";s:35:"Tint upcoming events activity icons";s:30:"upcomingeventstintenabled_desc";s:170:"With this setting, you can tint the activity icons in the upcoming events block based on the activity purposes. By default, Moodle core displays them just as black icons.";s:28:"recentlyaccesseditemsheading";s:29:"Recently accessed items block";s:32:"recentlyaccesseditemstintenabled";s:43:"Tint recently accessed items activity icons";s:37:"recentlyaccesseditemstintenabled_desc";s:178:"With this setting, you can tint the activity icons in the recently accessed items block based on the activity purposes. By default, Moodle core displays them just as black icons.";s:17:"activitiesheading";s:16:"Activities block";s:21:"activitiestintenabled";s:30:"Tint activities activity icons";s:26:"activitiestintenabled_desc";s:165:"With this setting, you can tint the activity icons in the activities block based on the activity purposes. By default, Moodle core displays them just as black icons.";s:9:"coursetab";s:6:"Course";s:19:"courseheaderheading";s:13:"Course Header";s:24:"courseheaderimageenabled";s:45:"Display the course image in the course header";s:29:"courseheaderimageenabled_desc";s:224:"When enabled, the course image (which can be uploaded in a course's course settings) is displayed in the header of a course. The course images are shown there in addition to the 'My courses' page where they are always shown.";s:25:"courseheaderimagefallback";s:28:"Fallback course header image";s:30:"courseheaderimagefallback_desc";s:349:"If you upload an image in this setting, it is used as fallback image and is displayed in the course header if no course image is uploaded in a particular course's course settings. If you do not upload an image here, a course header image is only shown in a particular course if a course image is uploaded in this particular course's course settings.";s:23:"courseheaderimageheight";s:26:"Course header image height";s:28:"courseheaderimageheight_desc";s:79:"With this setting, you control the height of the presented course header image.";s:23:"courseheaderimagelayout";s:26:"Course header image layout";s:28:"courseheaderimagelayout_desc";s:90:"With this setting, you control the layout of the course header image and the course title.";s:34:"courseheaderimagelayoutstackeddark";s:82:"Course title stacked on course image (white font color for dark background images)";s:35:"courseheaderimagelayoutstackedlight";s:83:"Course title stacked on course image (black font color for light background images)";s:35:"courseheaderimagelayoutheadingabove";s:34:"Course title above of course image";s:25:"courseheaderimageposition";s:28:"Course header image position";s:30:"courseheaderimageposition_desc";s:202:"With this setting, you control the positioning of the course header image within the course header image container. The first value is the horizontal position, the second value is the vertical position.";s:18:"courseindexheading";s:12:"Course Index";s:25:"courseindexmodiconenabled";s:43:"Display activity type icons in course index";s:30:"courseindexmodiconenabled_desc";s:327:"When enabled, the corresponding activity type icon is displayed in front of the index row with the title of the activity. In doing so, the course activity type is either replacing the course completion indicator which is moved from the front to the end of the course index row line, or colored in by the completion state color.";s:33:"courseindexcompletioninfoposition";s:42:"Position of activity completion indication";s:38:"courseindexcompletioninfoposition_desc";s:428:"Choose the position where the completion indication is displayed. <em>End of line</em> displays the standard completion indicator at the end of the course index row line. <em>Start of line</em> displays the standard completion indicator at the start of the course index row line. <em>Icon color</em> does not show the standard completion indicator, but encodes the completion information as background of the course module icon.";s:42:"courseindexcompletioninfopositionendofline";s:11:"End of line";s:42:"courseindexcompletioninfopositioniconcolor";s:10:"Icon color";s:44:"courseindexcompletioninfopositionstartofline";s:13:"Start of line";s:16:"emailbrandingtab";s:15:"E-Mail branding";s:23:"templateemailhtmlprefix";s:0:"";s:23:"templateemailhtmlsuffix";s:0:"";s:23:"templateemailtextprefix";s:0:"";s:23:"templateemailtextsuffix";s:0:"";s:25:"emailbrandingintroheading";s:12:"Introduction";s:22:"emailbrandingintronote";s:150:"Please note: This is an advanced functionality which uses some workarounds to provide E-Mail branding options. Please follow the instructions closely.";s:24:"emailbrandinginstruction";s:6:"How-to";s:25:"emailbrandinginstruction0";s:97:"With this Boost Union feature, you can apply branding to all E-Mails which Moodle is sending out.";s:27:"emailbrandinginstructionli1";s:145:"Go to the <a href="{$a->url}" target="_blank">language customization settings page</a> to open the <em>{$a->lang}</em> language pack for editing.";s:27:"emailbrandinginstructionli2";s:88:"Search for and modify these strings in the <code>theme_boost_union</code> language pack:";s:30:"emailbrandinginstructionli2li1";s:166:"<code>templateemailhtmlprefix</code>: This snippet will be added <em>at the beginning / before the body</em> of all <em>HTML E-Mails</em> which Moodle is sending out.";s:30:"emailbrandinginstructionli2li2";s:159:"<code>templateemailhtmlsuffix</code>: This snippet will be added <em>at the end / after the body</em> of all <em>HTML E-Mails</em> which Moodle is sending out.";s:30:"emailbrandinginstructionli2li3";s:171:"<code>templateemailtextprefix</code>: This snippet will be added <em>at the beginning / before the body</em> of all <em>plaintext E-Mails</em> which Moodle is sending out.";s:30:"emailbrandinginstructionli2li4";s:164:"<code>templateemailtextsuffix</code>: This snippet will be added <em>at the end / after the body</em> of all <em>plaintext E-Mails</em> which Moodle is sending out.";s:27:"emailbrandinginstructionli3";s:38:"Save the changes to the language pack.";s:27:"emailbrandinginstructionli4";s:68:"Come back to this page and have a look at the E-Mail previews below.";s:21:"emailbrandingpitfalls";s:8:"Pitfalls";s:22:"emailbrandingpitfalls0";s:73:"Using this feature, there are some pitfalls which you should be aware of:";s:24:"emailbrandingpitfallsli1";s:222:"It is mandatory that you modify the language pack strings of the <em>current default language</em> of this site. Even if you have multiple language packs installed, only changes to the default language will have an effect.";s:24:"emailbrandingpitfallsli2";s:136:"Respecting the receipient's language is not possible. Thus, you should use language-agnostic terms within your E-Mail branding snippets.";s:24:"emailbrandingpitfallsli3";s:155:"If you ever change the site's default language in the future, you will have to migrate the modified language pack strings to the new default language pack.";s:24:"emailbrandingpitfallsli4";s:253:"In plaintext E-Mails, there is a line break and an empty line added automatically after the prefix and an empty line added automatically before the suffix snippet. This is to make sure that the suffix and prefix do not stick directly to the E-Mail body.";s:24:"emailbrandingpitfallsli5";s:227:"In HTML E-Mails, the prefix and the suffix are directly added before and above the E-Mail body. This is to make sure that you can work with HTML tags easily, however you will have to handle all spacing around the body yourself.";s:24:"emailbrandingpitfallsli6";s:178:"In HTML E-Mails, you can open a HTML tag in the prefix snippet and close the tag in the suffix snippet without problems. Just remember to create valid HTML in the resulting mail.";s:24:"emailbrandinghtmlheading";s:19:"HTML E-Mail preview";s:22:"emailbrandinghtmlintro";s:124:"This is a preview of a HTML E-Mail based on the branding prefixes and suffixes which are currently set in the language pack.";s:26:"emailbrandinghtmlnopreview";s:120:"Up to now, the HTML E-Mails haven't been customized within this feature. E-Mails will be composed and sent out normally.";s:25:"emailbrandinghtmldemobody";s:537:"<p>E-Mail body starts here.</p><p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua.</p><p>Id donec ultrices tincidunt arcu non sodales. Id volutpat lacus laoreet non curabitur gravida arcu.</p><p>Cursus turpis massa tincidunt dui. Pellentesque nec nam aliquam sem et tortor consequat id. In ornare quam viverra orci sagittis eu volutpat. Sem nulla pharetra diam sit amet nisl suscipit. Justo donec enim diam vulputate ut pharetra.</p><p>E-Mail body ends here.</p>";s:24:"emailbrandingtextheading";s:24:"Plaintext E-Mail preview";s:22:"emailbrandingtextintro";s:129:"This is a preview of a plaintext E-Mail based on the branding prefixes and suffixes which are currently set in the language pack.";s:26:"emailbrandingtextnopreview";s:125:"Up to now, the plaintext E-Mails haven't been customized within this feature. E-Mails will be composed and sent out normally.";s:25:"emailbrandingtextdemobody";s:510:"E-Mail body starts here.

Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua.

Id donec ultrices tincidunt arcu non sodales. Id volutpat lacus laoreet non curabitur gravida arcu.

Cursus turpis massa tincidunt dui. Pellentesque nec nam aliquam sem et tortor consequat id. In ornare quam viverra orci sagittis eu volutpat. Sem nulla pharetra diam sit amet nisl suscipit. Justo donec enim diam vulputate ut pharetra.

E-Mail body ends here.";s:12:"resourcestab";s:9:"Resources";s:25:"resourcescachecontrolnote";s:526:"Please note that the files are shipped to the browser with the 'Cache-Control' header set which tells the browser to cache the file. If you are sure that you won't change the file in the near future, you can use the persistent URL to link to the file. However, if you plan to modify a file but keep the same filename every now and then, you should rather use the revisioned URL and re-link the file where you have used it everytime you update the file to avoid that the browsers will show cached outdated versions of the file.";s:26:"additionalresourcesheading";s:20:"Additional resources";s:26:"additionalresourcessetting";s:20:"Additional resources";s:31:"additionalresourcessetting_desc";s:551:"With this setting you can upload additional resources to the theme. The advantage of uploading files to this file area is that those files can be delivered without a check if the user is logged in. This is also why you should only add files that are uncritical and everyone should be allowed to access and don't need be protected with a valid login. As soon as you have uploaded at least one file to this filearea and have stored the settings, a list will appear underneath which will give you the URL which you can use to reference a particular file.";s:30:"additionalresourceslistsetting";s:25:"Additional resources list";s:35:"additionalresourceslistsetting_desc";s:260:"This is the list of files which you have uploaded to the additional resources filearea. The given URLs can be used to link to these files from within your custom CSS, from the footnote or wherever you need to use uploaded files but can't upload files in place.";s:36:"additionalresourcesfileurlpersistent";s:16:"URL (persistent)";s:36:"additionalresourcesfileurlrevisioned";s:16:"URL (revisioned)";s:18:"customfontsheading";s:12:"Custom fonts";s:18:"customfontssetting";s:12:"Custom fonts";s:23:"customfontssetting_desc";s:503:"With this setting you can upload custom fonts to the theme. The advantage of uploading fonts to this file area is that those fonts can be delivered without a check if the user is logged in and can be used as locally installed fonts everywhere on the site. As soon as you have uploaded at least one font to this filearea and have stored the settings, a list will appear underneath which will give you CSS code snippets which you can use as a boilerplate to reference particular fonts in your custom SCSS.";s:22:"customfontslistsetting";s:17:"Custom fonts list";s:27:"customfontslistsetting_desc";s:366:"This is the list of fonts which you have uploaded to the custom fonts filearea. The given CSS snippets can be used to add these fonts to your custom SCSS. Please note that you will have to take care of the font format value as well as the font-family, font-style and font-weight CSS properties yourself for now as Boost Union is not able yet to parse the font files.";s:6:"h5ptab";s:3:"H5P";s:13:"cssh5pheading";s:15:"Raw CSS for H5P";s:13:"cssh5psetting";s:15:"Raw CSS for H5P";s:18:"cssh5psetting_desc";s:189:"Use this field to provide CSS code which will be applied to the presentation of H5P content by mod_h5p and mod_hvp. Please inspect the H5P content types to find the necessary CSS selectors.";s:19:"contentwidthheading";s:13:"Content width";s:25:"h5pcontentmaxwidthsetting";s:26:"H5P content bank max width";s:30:"h5pcontentmaxwidthsetting_desc";s:434:"With this setting, you can override Moodle's H5P content bank width without manual SCSS modifications. This width is used for the H5P editor within the content bank. It is <em>not</em> used for the width of the H5P activity. By default, Moodle uses a H5P content bank max width of 960px. You can enter other pixel-based values like 1200px, but you can also enter a percentage-based value like 100% or a viewport-width value like 90vw.";s:9:"mobiletab";s:6:"Mobile";s:16:"mobileappheading";s:10:"Mobile app";s:9:"mobilecss";s:29:"Additional CSS for Mobile app";s:14:"mobilecss_desc";s:375:"With this setting, you can write custom CSS code to customise your mobile app interface. The CSS code will be only added to the Mobile app depiction of this Moodle instance and will not be shown in the webbrowser version. Read more about this feature in the <a href="https://moodledev.io/general/app/customisation/remote-themes#how-do-remote-themes-work">Moodle dev docs</a>.";s:13:"mobilecss_set";s:200:"As soon as you add any CSS code to this setting and save the setting, the <a href="{$a->url}">Moodle core setting <em>mobilecssurl</em></a> will be automatically set to a URL of the Boost Union theme.";s:19:"mobilecss_overwrite";s:282:"As soon as you add any CSS code to this setting and save the setting, the <a href="{$a->url}">Moodle core setting <em>mobilecssurl</em></a> will be automatically overwritten with a URL of the Boost Union theme. Currently this setting is set to <a href="{$a->value}">{$a->value}</a>.";s:21:"mobilecss_donotchange";s:163:"This step is necessary to ship the CSS code to the Mobile app. Do not change the URL there unless you really want to remove the CSS code from the Mobile app again.";s:23:"mobileappearanceheading";s:17:"Mobile appearance";s:17:"touchiconfilesios";s:24:"Touch icon files for iOS";s:22:"touchiconfilesios_desc";s:146:"Within this setting, you can upload files which are used as homescreen icon as soon as the Moodle site is added to the iOS homescreen as bookmark.";s:29:"touchiconfilesios_recommended";s:26:"Recommended files for iOS:";s:26:"touchiconfilesios_optional";s:23:"Optional files for iOS:";s:25:"touchiconfilesios_example";s:40:"Example filename: apple-icon-152x152.png";s:22:"touchiconfilesios_note";s:279:"Recommended files have a good size to be shown properly on current iOS devices and should be provided. Optional files are (or have been previously) supported by iOS devices as well but should be really considered as optional unless you have a particular legacy device to support.";s:21:"touchiconfilesioslist";s:29:"Touch icon files for iOS list";s:26:"touchiconfilesioslist_desc";s:91:"This is the list of files which you have uploaded to the touch icon files for iOS filearea.";s:35:"touchiconlistiosrecommendeduploaded";s:87:"This is a recommended file to be used as touch icon on iOS devices and it was uploaded.";s:34:"touchiconlistiosrecommendedmissing";s:101:"This is a recommended file to be used as touch icon on iOS devices, but it was not uploaded properly.";s:32:"touchiconlistiosoptionaluploaded";s:85:"This is an optional file to be used as touch icon on iOS devices and it was uploaded.";s:31:"touchiconlistiosoptionalmissing";s:89:"This is an optional file to be used as touch icon on iOS devices and it was not uploaded.";s:15:"configtitlefeel";s:4:"Feel";s:13:"navigationtab";s:10:"Navigation";s:24:"primarynavigationheading";s:18:"Primary navigation";s:33:"hidenodesprimarynavigationsetting";s:32:"Hide nodes in primary navigation";s:38:"hidenodesprimarynavigationsetting_desc";s:285:"With this setting, you can hide one or multiple nodes from the primary navigation.<br /><br />
Please note: Here, you can just remove navigation nodes. But if you want to add custom navigation nodes, please consider using <a href="{$a->url}">Boost Union's smart menu functionality</a>.";s:35:"hidenodesprimarynavigationonlyguest";s:33:"This node is shown to guests only";s:29:"alternativelogolinkurlsetting";s:25:"Alternative logo link URL";s:34:"alternativelogolinkurlsetting_desc";s:314:"With this setting, you can set an alternative link URL which will be used as link on the logo in the navigation bar. You can use this setting to, for example, link to your organization's website instead of the Moodle frontpage to maintain a homogeneous navigation bar throughout all of your organization's systems.";s:15:"usermenuheading";s:9:"User menu";s:30:"showfullnameinusermenussetting";s:31:"Show full name in the user menu";s:35:"showfullnameinusermenussetting_desc";s:445:"With this setting, you can show the logged-in user's full name at the top of the user menu. This can be especially helpful for exam situations where teachers have to confirm that the user is logged in with his own account, but it might also be helpful for the user himself. In contrast to the Classic theme which shows the user's full name in the navbar near the avatar, this approach here does not claim any additional rare space in the navbar.";s:41:"showfullnameinusermenussetting_loggedinas";s:21:"You are logged in as:";s:23:"addpreferredlangsetting";s:44:"Add preferred language link to language menu";s:28:"addpreferredlangsetting_desc";s:358:"With this setting, you can add a 'Set preferred language' setting to the language menu within the user menu. Understandably, this setting is only processed if the setting <a href="{$a->url1}">Display language menu</a> is enabled, and if at least <a href="{$a->url2}">a second language pack is installed</a> and <a href="{$a->url3}">offered for selection</a>.";s:20:"setpreferredlanglink";s:22:"Set preferred language";s:22:"loginlinkbuttonenabled";s:31:"Display "Log in" link as button";s:27:"loginlinkbuttonenabled_desc";s:173:"With this setting, you can have the "Log in" link in the top of the page shown as button. This can help your users to recognize the fact they they are not logged in already.";s:31:"shownavbarstarredcoursessetting";s:42:"Show starred courses popover in the navbar";s:36:"shownavbarstarredcoursessetting_desc";s:122:"With this setting, you can show a popover menu with links to starred courses next to the messages and notifications menus.";s:31:"shownavbarstarredcourses_config";s:38:"Set starred courses on the '{$a}' page";s:30:"shownavbarstarredcourses_label";s:15:"Starred courses";s:31:"starredcourseslinktargetsetting";s:44:"Starred courses popover cog icon link target";s:36:"starredcourseslinktargetsetting_desc";s:284:"With this setting, you can set the link target of the cog icon in the starred courses popover. By default, the cog icon links to the 'My courses' page. However, you can also link to the 'Dashboard' page, especially if you have disabled the 'My courses' page in the primary navigation.";s:18:"breadcrumbsheading";s:11:"Breadcrumbs";s:19:"categorybreadcrumbs";s:53:"Display the category breadcrumbs in the course header";s:24:"categorybreadcrumbs_desc";s:203:"By default, the course category breadcrumbs are not shown on course pages in the course header. With this setting, you can show the course category breadcrumbs in the course header above the course name.";s:17:"navigationheading";s:10:"Navigation";s:9:"backtotop";s:11:"Back to top";s:22:"backtotopbuttonsetting";s:18:"Back to top button";s:27:"backtotopbuttonsetting_desc";s:275:"With this setting a back to top button will appear in the bottom right corner of the page as soon as the user scrolls down the page. A button like this existed already on Boost in Moodle Core until Moodle 3.11, but was removed in 4.0. With Boost Union, you can bring it back.";s:16:"scrollspysetting";s:10:"Scroll-spy";s:21:"scrollspysetting_desc";s:137:"With this setting, upon toggling edit mode on and off, the scroll position at where the user was when performing the toggle is preserved.";s:25:"activitynavigationsetting";s:38:"Activity & section navigation elements";s:30:"activitynavigationsetting_desc";s:460:"With this setting, the elements to jump to the previous and next activity/resource as well as the pull down menu to jump to a distinct activity/resource become displayed. Furthermore, within courses using the 'one section per page' mode, similar elements for the previous and next section are displayed as well. UI elements like this existed already on Boost in Moodle Core until Moodle 3.11, but were removed in 4.0. With Boost Union, you can bring them back.";s:9:"blockstab";s:6:"Blocks";s:20:"blocksgeneralheading";s:14:"General blocks";s:19:"blockregionsheading";s:24:"Additional block regions";s:24:"blockregionsheading_desc";s:2041:"<p>Boost Union provides a large number of additional block regions which can be used to add and show blocks over the whole Moodle page:</p>
<ul><li>The <em>Outside block regions</em> are placed on all four sides of the Moodle page. They can be used to show blocks which accompany the shown Moodle page but do not directly belong to the main content.</li>
<li>The <em>Header block region</em> is placed between the Outside (top) area and the main content area. It can be used to show a block as course header information.</li>
<li>The <em>Content block regions</em> are placed directly over and under the main content in the main content area. They can be used to add blocks to the course content flow.</li>
<li>The <em>Footer block regions</em> are placed at the bottom of the page between the Outside (bottom) area and the footnote. You have three footer regions available to build columns if necessary.</li>
<li>The <em>Off-canvas block region</em> is somehow special as it hovers over the whole Moodle page as a drawer. The drawer is opened by the 9-dots icon at the very right side of the navigation bar. You have three off-canvas regions available to build columns if necessary.</li></ul>
<p>Please note:</p>
<ul><li>By default, all additional block regions are disabled. Please enable the particular block regions on the particular page layouts according to your needs. Try to be as focused as possible – too many block regions could overwhelm end users.</li>
<li>As soon as an additional block region is enabled, it is visible for all authenticated users and editable by teachers and managers (depending on the fact if the particular user is allowed to edit the particular Moodle page, of course). But there are also theme/boost_union:viewregion* and theme/boost_union:editregion* capabilities which allow you to fine-tune the usage of each block region according to your needs.</li>
<li>The Outside (left), Outside (right), Content (upper), Content (lower) and Header block regions are not available for all page layouts.</li></ul>";s:32:"blockregionsheading_experimental";s:342:"Please note: The <em>Outside (left) and Outside (right) block regions</em> are fully working in the current state of implementation, but have to be <em>considered as experimental</em> as they do not wrap properly on medium width screens yet. Against this background, please use them with care. This issue will be fixed in an upcoming release.";s:19:"region-outside-left";s:14:"Outside (left)";s:18:"region-outside-top";s:13:"Outside (top)";s:21:"region-outside-bottom";s:16:"Outside (bottom)";s:20:"region-outside-right";s:15:"Outside (right)";s:20:"region-content-upper";s:15:"Content (upper)";s:20:"region-content-lower";s:15:"Content (lower)";s:18:"region-footer-left";s:13:"Footer (left)";s:19:"region-footer-right";s:14:"Footer (right)";s:20:"region-footer-center";s:15:"Footer (center)";s:13:"region-header";s:6:"Header";s:21:"region-offcanvas-left";s:17:"Off-canvas (left)";s:22:"region-offcanvas-right";s:18:"Off-canvas (right)";s:23:"region-offcanvas-center";s:19:"Off-canvas (center)";s:14:"closeoffcanvas";s:23:"Close Off-canvas drawer";s:13:"openoffcanvas";s:22:"Open Off-canvas drawer";s:21:"blockregionsforlayout";s:42:"Additional block regions for '{$a}' layout";s:26:"blockregionsforlayout_desc";s:81:"With this setting, you can enable additional block regions for the '{$a}' layout.";s:22:"blockregionsstickyonly";s:275:"Please note: This page layout is limited by Moodle core in such a way that blocks cannot be added directly on the page. However, as soon as you enable a block region here, <a href="{$a}" target="_blank">site-wide sticky blocks</a> will still be displayed on this page layout.";s:21:"outsideregionsheading";s:15:"Outside regions";s:26:"outsideregionsheading_desc";s:112:"Outside regions can not only be enabled with the layout settings above, their appearance can also be customized.";s:27:"blockregionoutsideleftwidth";s:46:"Block region width for 'Outside (left)' region";s:32:"blockregionoutsideleftwidth_desc";s:332:"With this setting, you can set the width of the 'Outside (left)' block region which is shown on the left hand side of the main content area. By default, Boost Union uses a width of 300px. You can enter other pixel-based values like 200px, but you can also enter a percentage-based value like 10% or a viewport-width value like 10vw.";s:28:"blockregionoutsiderightwidth";s:47:"Block region width for 'Outside (right)' region";s:33:"blockregionoutsiderightwidth_desc";s:334:"With this setting, you can set the width of the 'Outside (right)' block region which is shown on the right hand side of the main content area. By default, Boost Union uses a width of 300px. You can enter other pixel-based values like 200px, but you can also enter a percentage-based value like 10% or a viewport-width value like 10vw.";s:26:"blockregionoutsidetopwidth";s:45:"Block region width for 'Outside (top)' region";s:31:"blockregionoutsidetopwidth_desc";s:192:"With this setting, you can set the width of the 'Outside (top)' block region which is shown at the very top of the page. You can choose between full width, course content width and hero width.";s:28:"outsideregionswidthfullwidth";s:10:"Full width";s:37:"outsideregionswidthcoursecontentwidth";s:20:"Course content width";s:28:"outsideregionswidthherowidth";s:10:"Hero width";s:29:"blockregionoutsidebottomwidth";s:48:"Block region width for 'Outside (bottom)' region";s:34:"blockregionoutsidebottomwidth_desc";s:190:"With this setting, you can set the width of the 'Outside (bottom)' block region which is shown below the main content. You can choose between full width, course content width and hero width.";s:20:"footerregionsheading";s:14:"Footer regions";s:25:"footerregionsheading_desc";s:111:"Footer regions can not only be enabled with the layout settings above, their appearance can also be customized.";s:22:"blockregionfooterwidth";s:38:"Block region width for 'Footer' region";s:27:"blockregionfooterwidth_desc";s:142:"With this setting, you can set the width of the 'Footer' block region. You can choose between full width, course content width and hero width.";s:23:"outsideregionsplacement";s:36:"Outside regions horizontal placement";s:28:"outsideregionsplacement_desc";s:191:"With this setting, you can control if, on larger screens, the 'Outside (left)' and 'Outside (right)' block regions should be placed near the main content area or rather near the window edges.";s:38:"outsideregionsplacementnextmaincontent";s:84:"Display 'Outside (left)' and 'Outside (right)' regions next to the main content area";s:38:"outsideregionsplacementnearwindowedges";s:76:"Display 'Outside (left)' and 'Outside (right)' regions near the window edges";s:37:"sitehomerighthandblockdrawerbehaviour";s:33:"Site home right-hand block drawer";s:46:"showsitehomerighthandblockdraweronvisitsetting";s:50:"Show right-hand block drawer of site home on visit";s:51:"showsitehomerighthandblockdraweronvisitsetting_desc";s:225:"With this setting, the right-hand block drawer of site home will be displayed in its expanded state by default. This only applies to users who are not logged in and does not overwrite the toggle state of each individual user.";s:51:"showsitehomerighthandblockdraweronfirstloginsetting";s:56:"Show right-hand block drawer of site home on first login";s:56:"showsitehomerighthandblockdraweronfirstloginsetting_desc";s:238:"With this setting, the right-hand block drawer of site home will be displayed in its expanded state by default. This only applies to users who log in for the very first time and does not overwrite the toggle state of each individual user.";s:51:"showsitehomerighthandblockdraweronguestloginsetting";s:56:"Show right-hand block drawer of site home on guest login";s:56:"showsitehomerighthandblockdraweronguestloginsetting_desc";s:161:"With this setting, the right-hand block drawer of site home will be displayed in its expanded state by default. This only applies to users who log in as a guest.";s:14:"pagelayoutstab";s:12:"Page layouts";s:13:"policyheading";s:8:"Policies";s:31:"policyoverviewnavigationsetting";s:39:"Show navigation on policy overview page";s:36:"policyoverviewnavigationsetting_desc";s:209:"By default, the <a href="{$a->url}">policy overview page (provided by tool_policy)</a> does not show a navigation menu or footer. With this setting, you can show the primary navigation and footer on that page.";s:8:"linkstab";s:5:"Links";s:25:"speciallinksmarkupheading";s:20:"Special links markup";s:24:"markexternallinkssetting";s:19:"Mark external links";s:29:"markexternallinkssetting_desc";s:99:"Adds an "external link" icon after external links (which lead the user to a target outside Moodle).";s:29:"markexternallinksscopesetting";s:25:"Mark external links scope";s:34:"markexternallinksscopesetting_desc";s:327:"With this setting, you control the scope where Boost Union should mark external links. By default, Boost Union marks external links on the whole Moodle page and does its best to cover some edge-cases where adding the external link icon does not make much sense. However, you can also limit the scope to better avoid edge-cases.";s:31:"marklinksscopesetting_wholepage";s:17:"On the whole page";s:32:"marklinksscopesetting_coursemain";s:54:"Within the main content area of course main pages only";s:22:"markmailtolinkssetting";s:17:"Mark mailto links";s:27:"markmailtolinkssetting_desc";s:49:"Adds an "envelope" icon in front of mailto links.";s:27:"markmailtolinksscopesetting";s:23:"Mark mailto links scope";s:32:"markmailtolinksscopesetting_desc";s:212:"With this setting, you control the scope where Boost Union should mark mailto links. By default, Boost Union marks mailto links on the whole Moodle page. However, you can also limit the scope to avoid edge-cases.";s:22:"markbrokenlinkssetting";s:17:"Mark broken links";s:27:"markbrokenlinkssetting_desc";s:412:"Adds a "broken chain" icon in front of broken links (which lead to uploaded draft files which have not been properly processed) and marks the link in the bootstrap color for "danger". In contrast to the "Mark external links" and "Mark mailto links" settings, there is no possibility to limit the scope of this setting as marking broken links is an indicator that something is broken and has to be fixed manually.";s:7:"misctab";s:13:"Miscellaneous";s:17:"javascriptheading";s:10:"JavaScript";s:22:"javascriptdisabledhint";s:24:"JavaScript disabled hint";s:27:"javascriptdisabledhint_desc";s:185:"With this setting, a hint will appear at the top of the Moodle page if JavaScript is not enabled. This is particularly helpful as several Moodle features do not work without JavaScript.";s:26:"javascriptdisabledhinttext";s:178:"JavaScript is disabled in your browser.<br />Many features of Moodle will be not usable or will appear to be broken.<br />Please enable JavaScript for the full Moodle experience.";s:18:"configtitlecontent";s:7:"Content";s:9:"footertab";s:6:"Footer";s:15:"footnoteheading";s:8:"Footnote";s:15:"footnotesetting";s:8:"Footnote";s:20:"footnotesetting_desc";s:366:"Whatever you add to this textarea will be displayed at the end of a page, in the footer (not the floating footer) on every page which uses the layouts "drawers", "columns2" or "login". Content in this area could be for example the copyright, the terms of use or the name of your organisation. <br/> If you want to remove the footnote again, just empty the text area.";s:15:"footnotelayouts";s:25:"Page layouts for footnote";s:20:"footnotelayouts_desc";s:151:"With this setting, you can control on which page layouts the footnote is shown. If no layout is selected, the footnote will not be shown on any layout.";s:13:"footerheading";s:6:"Footer";s:18:"enablefooterbutton";s:13:"Enable footer";s:23:"enablefooterbutton_desc";s:417:"With "footer", the circle containing the question mark at the bottom of the page is meant.<br />Upon click, the user is presented with an overlay. Depending on the site configuration Moodle shows several links (like "Documentation for this page" or "Data retention summary") are shown in this overlay.<br />With this setting, you can control whether to show or to suppress the footer button at the bottom of the page.";s:23:"enablefooterbutton_note";s:420:"Please note: The content of the <a href="{$a->url}">Moodle core setting additionalhtmlfooter</a> is shown within the footer by default. But if you select "Hide on all devices" here to hide the footer entirely, the additionalhtmlfooter content would not be shown anywhere anymore. To overcome this limitation, Boost Union will move the additionalhtmlfooter content to be shown at the very bottom of the page in this case.";s:22:"enablefooterbuttonboth";s:36:"Enable on desktop, tablet and mobile";s:25:"enablefooterbuttondesktop";s:89:"Enable on desktop and tablet only, hide on mobile (unchanged as presented by Moodle core)";s:24:"enablefooterbuttonmobile";s:49:"Enable on mobile only, hide on desktop and tablet";s:24:"enablefooterbuttonhidden";s:19:"Hide on all devices";s:26:"footersuppressiconssetting";s:43:"Suppress icons in front of the footer links";s:31:"footersuppressiconssetting_desc";s:171:"With this setting, you can entirely suppress the icons in front of the footer links. 'Documentation for this page' has a book icon, 'Services and support' a life ring etc.";s:25:"footersuppresschatsetting";s:43:"Suppress 'Chat to course participants' link";s:30:"footersuppresschatsetting_desc";s:211:"With this setting, you can entirely suppress the 'Chat to course participants' link in the footer. This link would otherwise appear within courses as soon as a communication room is added in a course's settings.";s:25:"footersuppresshelpsetting";s:43:"Suppress 'Documentation for this page' link";s:30:"footersuppresshelpsetting_desc";s:194:"With this setting, you can entirely suppress the 'Documentation for this page' link in the footer. This link would otherwise appear if a <a href="{$a->url}">Moodle Docs document root</a> is set.";s:29:"footersuppressservicessetting";s:36:"Suppress 'Services and support' link";s:34:"footersuppressservicessetting_desc";s:195:"With this setting, you can entirely suppress the 'Services and support' link in the footer. This link would otherwise show the <a href="{$a->url}">Services and support link</a> to administrators.";s:28:"footersuppresscontactsetting";s:36:"Suppress 'Contact site support' link";s:33:"footersuppresscontactsetting_desc";s:189:"With this setting, you can entirely suppress the 'Contact site support' link in the footer. This link would otherwise appear if the <a href="{$a->url}">Contact site support link</a> is set.";s:30:"footersuppresslogininfosetting";s:19:"Suppress Login info";s:35:"footersuppresslogininfosetting_desc";s:155:"With this setting, you can entirely suppress the login info in the footer. This info would otherwise show links to a user's profile and to the logout page.";s:29:"footersuppressusertoursetting";s:44:"Suppress 'Reset user tour on this page' link";s:34:"footersuppressusertoursetting_desc";s:192:"With this setting, you can entirely suppress the 'Reset user tour on this page' link in the footer. This link would otherwise provide the possibility to reset a user tour on a particular page.";s:32:"footersuppressthemeswitchsetting";s:29:"Suppress theme switcher links";s:37:"footersuppressthemeswitchsetting_desc";s:231:"With this setting, you can entirely suppress the theme switcher links in the footer. The underlying system for device-specific themes was removed in Moodle 4.3, but the output routines are still there, so better be save than sorry.";s:28:"footersuppresspoweredsetting";s:33:"Suppress 'Powered by Moodle' link";s:33:"footersuppresspoweredsetting_desc";s:200:"With this setting, you can entirely suppress the 'Powered by Moodle' link in the footer. This link would otherwise show an information that this site is running Moodle and provide a link to Moodle HQ.";s:32:"footersuppressstandardfootercore";s:47:"Suppress footer output by core component '{$a}'";s:37:"footersuppressstandardfootercore_desc";s:315:"With this setting, you can entirely suppress the footer output by the core component '{$a}'. Core components can add additional content to the footer by implementing a particular hook or function. This core component has implemented this hook / function and might add content to the footer in certain circumstances.";s:28:"footersuppressstandardfooter";s:39:"Suppress footer output by plugin '{$a}'";s:33:"footersuppressstandardfooter_desc";s:531:"With this setting, you can entirely suppress the footer output by plugin '{$a}'. Plugins (even if they are shipped with Moodle core, but are still technically plugins) can add additional content to the footer by implementing a particular hook or function. This plugin has implemented this hook / function and might add content to the footer in certain circumstances.<br />Please note: Due to the way how the suppressing feature is implemented, the setting might not take effect before the second page load after saving the setting.";s:48:"footersuppressstandardfooter_configoverride_desc";s:248:"The footer output by plugin '{$a}' is already suppressed via <code>$CFG->hooks_callback_overrides</code> in your <code>config.php</code> file. To make this setting configurable here, you need to remove your override in <code>config.php</code> file.";s:14:"staticpagestab";s:12:"Static pages";s:14:"aboutusheading";s:8:"About us";s:20:"enableaboutussetting";s:20:"Enable about us page";s:15:"aboutusdisabled";s:74:"The about us page is disabled for this site. There is nothing to see here.";s:21:"aboutuscontentsetting";s:16:"About us content";s:26:"aboutuscontentsetting_desc";s:88:"In this setting, you can add rich text content which will be shown on the about us page.";s:23:"aboutuspagetitledefault";s:8:"About us";s:23:"aboutuspagetitlesetting";s:19:"About us page title";s:28:"aboutuspagetitlesetting_desc";s:183:"In this setting, you can define the title of the about us page. This text will be used as link text to the about us page as well if you configure 'About us link position' accordingly.";s:23:"aboutuslinkpositionnone";s:53:"Do not automatically show a link to the about us page";s:27:"aboutuslinkpositionfootnote";s:47:"Add a link to the about us page to the footnote";s:25:"aboutuslinkpositionfooter";s:65:"Add a link to the about us page to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:23:"aboutuslinkpositionboth";s:85:"Add a link to the about us page to the footnote and to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:26:"aboutuslinkpositionsetting";s:22:"About us link position";s:31:"aboutuslinkpositionsetting_desc";s:230:"In this setting, you can configure if a link to the about us page should be added automatically to the Moodle page. If you do not want to show a link automatically, you can add a link to {$a->url} from anywhere in Moodle manually.";s:13:"offersheading";s:6:"Offers";s:19:"enableofferssetting";s:18:"Enable offers page";s:14:"offersdisabled";s:72:"The offers page is disabled for this site. There is nothing to see here.";s:20:"offerscontentsetting";s:14:"Offers content";s:25:"offerscontentsetting_desc";s:86:"In this setting, you can add rich text content which will be shown on the offers page.";s:22:"offerspagetitledefault";s:6:"Offers";s:22:"offerspagetitlesetting";s:17:"Offers page title";s:27:"offerspagetitlesetting_desc";s:177:"In this setting, you can define the title of the offers page. This text will be used as link text to the offers page as well if you configure 'Offers link position' accordingly.";s:22:"offerslinkpositionnone";s:51:"Do not automatically show a link to the offers page";s:26:"offerslinkpositionfootnote";s:45:"Add a link to the offers page to the footnote";s:24:"offerslinkpositionfooter";s:63:"Add a link to the offers page to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:22:"offerslinkpositionboth";s:83:"Add a link to the offers page to the footnote and to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:25:"offerslinkpositionsetting";s:20:"Offers link position";s:30:"offerslinkpositionsetting_desc";s:228:"In this setting, you can configure if a link to the offers page should be added automatically to the Moodle page. If you do not want to show a link automatically, you can add a link to {$a->url} from anywhere in Moodle manually.";s:14:"imprintheading";s:7:"Imprint";s:20:"enableimprintsetting";s:14:"Enable imprint";s:15:"imprintdisabled";s:73:"The imprint page is disabled for this site. There is nothing to see here.";s:21:"imprintcontentsetting";s:15:"Imprint content";s:26:"imprintcontentsetting_desc";s:87:"In this setting, you can add rich text content which will be shown on the imprint page.";s:23:"imprintpagetitledefault";s:7:"Imprint";s:23:"imprintpagetitlesetting";s:18:"Imprint page title";s:28:"imprintpagetitlesetting_desc";s:180:"In this setting, you can define the title of the imprint page. This text will be used as link text to the imprint page as well if you configure 'Imprint link position' accordingly.";s:23:"imprintlinkpositionnone";s:52:"Do not automatically show a link to the imprint page";s:27:"imprintlinkpositionfootnote";s:46:"Add a link to the imprint page to the footnote";s:25:"imprintlinkpositionfooter";s:64:"Add a link to the imprint page to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:23:"imprintlinkpositionboth";s:84:"Add a link to the imprint page to the footnote and to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:26:"imprintlinkpositionsetting";s:21:"Imprint link position";s:31:"imprintlinkpositionsetting_desc";s:229:"In this setting, you can configure if a link to the imprint page should be added automatically to the Moodle page. If you do not want to show a link automatically, you can add a link to {$a->url} from anywhere in Moodle manually.";s:14:"contactheading";s:7:"Contact";s:20:"enablecontactsetting";s:19:"Enable contact page";s:15:"contactdisabled";s:73:"The contact page is disabled for this site. There is nothing to see here.";s:21:"contactcontentsetting";s:20:"Contact page content";s:26:"contactcontentsetting_desc";s:160:"In this setting, you can add rich text content which will be shown on a contact page (which is not the same as the built-in Moodle 'Contact site support' page).";s:23:"contactpagetitledefault";s:7:"Contact";s:23:"contactpagetitlesetting";s:18:"Contact page title";s:28:"contactpagetitlesetting_desc";s:185:"In this setting, you can define the title of the contact page. This text will be used as link text to the contact page as well if you configure 'Contact page link position' accordingly.";s:23:"contactlinkpositionnone";s:52:"Do not automatically show a link to the contact page";s:27:"contactlinkpositionfootnote";s:46:"Add a link to the contact page to the footnote";s:25:"contactlinkpositionfooter";s:64:"Add a link to the contact page to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:23:"contactlinkpositionboth";s:84:"Add a link to the contact page to the footnote and to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:26:"contactlinkpositionsetting";s:26:"Contact page link position";s:31:"contactlinkpositionsetting_desc";s:229:"In this setting, you can configure if a link to the contact page should be added automatically to the Moodle page. If you do not want to show a link automatically, you can add a link to {$a->url} from anywhere in Moodle manually.";s:11:"helpheading";s:4:"Help";s:17:"enablehelpsetting";s:16:"Enable help page";s:12:"helpdisabled";s:70:"The help page is disabled for this site. There is nothing to see here.";s:18:"helpcontentsetting";s:17:"Help page content";s:23:"helpcontentsetting_desc";s:82:"In this setting, you can add rich text content which will be shown on a help page.";s:20:"helppagetitledefault";s:4:"Help";s:20:"helppagetitlesetting";s:15:"Help page title";s:25:"helppagetitlesetting_desc";s:176:"In this setting, you can define the title of the help page. This text will be used as link text to the help page as well if you configure 'Help page link position' accordingly.";s:20:"helplinkpositionnone";s:49:"Do not automatically show a link to the help page";s:24:"helplinkpositionfootnote";s:43:"Add a link to the help page to the footnote";s:22:"helplinkpositionfooter";s:61:"Add a link to the help page to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:20:"helplinkpositionboth";s:81:"Add a link to the help page to the footnote and to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:23:"helplinkpositionsetting";s:23:"Help page link position";s:28:"helplinkpositionsetting_desc";s:226:"In this setting, you can configure if a link to the help page should be added automatically to the Moodle page. If you do not want to show a link automatically, you can add a link to {$a->url} from anywhere in Moodle manually.";s:18:"maintenanceheading";s:11:"Maintenance";s:24:"enablemaintenancesetting";s:35:"Enable maintenance information page";s:19:"maintenancedisabled";s:89:"The maintenance information page is disabled for this site. There is nothing to see here.";s:25:"maintenancecontentsetting";s:36:"Maintenance information page content";s:30:"maintenancecontentsetting_desc";s:170:"In this setting, you can add rich text content which will be shown on a maintenance information page (which is not the same as the built-in Moodle maintenance mode page).";s:27:"maintenancepagetitledefault";s:11:"Maintenance";s:27:"maintenancepagetitlesetting";s:34:"Maintenance information page title";s:32:"maintenancepagetitlesetting_desc";s:233:"In this setting, you can define the title of the maintenance information page. This text will be used as link text to the maintenance information page as well if you configure 'Maintenance information page link position' accordingly.";s:27:"maintenancelinkpositionnone";s:68:"Do not automatically show a link to the maintenance information page";s:31:"maintenancelinkpositionfootnote";s:62:"Add a link to the maintenance information page to the footnote";s:29:"maintenancelinkpositionfooter";s:80:"Add a link to the maintenance information page to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:27:"maintenancelinkpositionboth";s:100:"Add a link to the maintenance information page to the footnote and to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:30:"maintenancelinkpositionsetting";s:42:"Maintenance information page link position";s:35:"maintenancelinkpositionsetting_desc";s:245:"In this setting, you can configure if a link to the maintenance information page should be added automatically to the Moodle page. If you do not want to show a link automatically, you can add a link to {$a->url} from anywhere in Moodle manually.";s:12:"page1heading";s:14:"Generic page 1";s:18:"enablepage1setting";s:21:"Enable generic page 1";s:13:"page1disabled";s:75:"The generic page 1 is disabled for this site. There is nothing to see here.";s:19:"page1contentsetting";s:22:"Generic page 1 content";s:24:"page1contentsetting_desc";s:89:"In this setting, you can add rich text content which will be shown on the generic page 1.";s:21:"page1pagetitledefault";s:14:"Generic page 1";s:21:"page1pagetitlesetting";s:20:"Generic page 1 title";s:26:"page1pagetitlesetting_desc";s:191:"In this setting, you can define the title of the generic page 1. This text will be used as link text to the generic page 1 as well if you configure 'Generic page 1 link position' accordingly.";s:21:"page1linkpositionnone";s:54:"Do not automatically show a link to the generic page 1";s:25:"page1linkpositionfootnote";s:48:"Add a link to the generic page 1 to the footnote";s:23:"page1linkpositionfooter";s:66:"Add a link to the generic page 1 to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:21:"page1linkpositionboth";s:86:"Add a link to the generic page 1 to the footnote and to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:24:"page1linkpositionsetting";s:28:"Generic page 1 link position";s:29:"page1linkpositionsetting_desc";s:231:"In this setting, you can configure if a link to the generic page 1 should be added automatically to the Moodle page. If you do not want to show a link automatically, you can add a link to {$a->url} from anywhere in Moodle manually.";s:12:"page2heading";s:14:"Generic page 2";s:18:"enablepage2setting";s:21:"Enable generic page 2";s:13:"page2disabled";s:75:"The generic page 2 is disabled for this site. There is nothing to see here.";s:19:"page2contentsetting";s:22:"Generic page 2 content";s:24:"page2contentsetting_desc";s:89:"In this setting, you can add rich text content which will be shown on the generic page 2.";s:21:"page2pagetitledefault";s:14:"Generic page 2";s:21:"page2pagetitlesetting";s:20:"Generic page 2 title";s:26:"page2pagetitlesetting_desc";s:191:"In this setting, you can define the title of the generic page 2. This text will be used as link text to the generic page 2 as well if you configure 'Generic page 2 link position' accordingly.";s:21:"page2linkpositionnone";s:54:"Do not automatically show a link to the generic page 2";s:25:"page2linkpositionfootnote";s:48:"Add a link to the generic page 2 to the footnote";s:23:"page2linkpositionfooter";s:66:"Add a link to the generic page 2 to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:21:"page2linkpositionboth";s:86:"Add a link to the generic page 2 to the footnote and to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:24:"page2linkpositionsetting";s:28:"Generic page 2 link position";s:29:"page2linkpositionsetting_desc";s:231:"In this setting, you can configure if a link to the generic page 2 should be added automatically to the Moodle page. If you do not want to show a link automatically, you can add a link to {$a->url} from anywhere in Moodle manually.";s:12:"page3heading";s:14:"Generic page 3";s:18:"enablepage3setting";s:21:"Enable generic page 3";s:13:"page3disabled";s:75:"The generic page 3 is disabled for this site. There is nothing to see here.";s:19:"page3contentsetting";s:22:"Generic page 3 content";s:24:"page3contentsetting_desc";s:89:"In this setting, you can add rich text content which will be shown on the generic page 3.";s:21:"page3pagetitledefault";s:14:"Generic page 3";s:21:"page3pagetitlesetting";s:20:"Generic page 3 title";s:26:"page3pagetitlesetting_desc";s:191:"In this setting, you can define the title of the generic page 3. This text will be used as link text to the generic page 3 as well if you configure 'Generic page 3 link position' accordingly.";s:21:"page3linkpositionnone";s:54:"Do not automatically show a link to the generic page 3";s:25:"page3linkpositionfootnote";s:48:"Add a link to the generic page 3 to the footnote";s:23:"page3linkpositionfooter";s:66:"Add a link to the generic page 3 to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:21:"page3linkpositionboth";s:86:"Add a link to the generic page 3 to the footnote and to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:24:"page3linkpositionsetting";s:28:"Generic page 3 link position";s:29:"page3linkpositionsetting_desc";s:231:"In this setting, you can configure if a link to the generic page 3 should be added automatically to the Moodle page. If you do not want to show a link automatically, you can add a link to {$a->url} from anywhere in Moodle manually.";s:13:"infobannertab";s:11:"Info banner";s:17:"infobannerheading";s:20:"Info banner {$a->no}";s:23:"infobannerpageloginpage";s:10:"Login page";s:23:"infobannermodeperpetual";s:9:"Perpetual";s:23:"infobannermodetimebased";s:15:"Time controlled";s:21:"bootstrapprimarycolor";s:13:"Primary color";s:23:"bootstrapsecondarycolor";s:15:"Secondary color";s:21:"bootstrapsuccesscolor";s:13:"Success color";s:20:"bootstrapdangercolor";s:12:"Danger color";s:21:"bootstrapwarningcolor";s:13:"Warning color";s:18:"bootstrapinfocolor";s:10:"Info color";s:19:"bootstraplightcolor";s:11:"Light color";s:18:"bootstrapdarkcolor";s:10:"Dark color";s:13:"bootstrapnone";s:18:"No Bootstrap color";s:15:"infobannerclose";s:5:"Close";s:22:"infobannerdismissreset";s:41:"Reset visibility of dismissed info banner";s:28:"infobannerdismissresetbutton";s:40:"Reset visibility of info banner {$a->no}";s:24:"infobannerdismissconfirm";s:126:"Do you really want to reset the visibility of info banner {$a->no} and want to re-show it for all users who have dismissed it?";s:24:"infobannerdismisssuccess";s:53:"The visibility of info banner {$a->no} has been reset";s:21:"infobannerdismissfail";s:77:"The visibility reset of info banner {$a->no} has failed for at least one user";s:33:"error:infobannerdismissnonotvalid";s:41:"The given info banner number is not valid";s:39:"error:infobannerdismissnonotdismissible";s:40:"The given info banner is not dismissible";s:24:"infobannerenabledsetting";s:27:"Enable info banner {$a->no}";s:29:"infobannerenabledsetting_desc";s:55:"With this setting, you can enable info banner {$a->no}.";s:24:"infobannercontentsetting";s:28:"Info banner {$a->no} content";s:29:"infobannercontentsetting_desc";s:82:"Here, you enter the information which should be shown within info banner {$a->no}.";s:22:"infobannerpagessetting";s:47:"Page layouts to display info banner {$a->no} on";s:27:"infobannerpagessetting_desc";s:101:"With this setting, you can select the page layouts on which info banner {$a->no} should be displayed.";s:24:"infobannerbsclasssetting";s:36:"Info banner {$a->no} Bootstrap class";s:29:"infobannerbsclasssetting_desc";s:309:"With this setting, you can select the Bootstrap style with which info banner {$a->no} should be displayed. If you choose the 'No Bootstrap color' option, the info banner will be output without any particular Bootstrap color which gives you the freedom to style the banner yourself within the rich-text editor.";s:22:"infobannerordersetting";s:35:"Info banner {$a->no} order position";s:27:"infobannerordersetting_desc";s:402:"With this setting, you define the order position of info banner {$a->no}. By default, the info banners are ordered from top to bottom like you see them on this settings page here. However, you can decide to assign another order position with this setting. If you assign the same order position to two or more information banners, they will be ordered again according to the order on this settings page.";s:21:"infobannermodesetting";s:33:"Info banner {$a->no} display mode";s:26:"infobannermodesetting_desc";s:196:"With this setting, you can define if info banner {$a->no} should be a perpetual banner (which is always shown) or a time controlled banner (which is only shown within the configured time interval)";s:28:"infobannerdismissiblesetting";s:32:"Info banner {$a->no} dismissible";s:33:"infobannerdismissiblesetting_desc";s:373:"With this setting, you can make info banner {$a->no} dismissible. If the user clicks on the x-button in the info banner, the banner will be hidden for this user permanently. The visibility is not reset anyhow automatically, even if you change the content of the info banner. If you want to reset the visibility of the info banner, click the 'Reset visibility' button below.";s:22:"infobannerstartsetting";s:31:"Info banner {$a->no} start time";s:27:"infobannerstartsetting_desc";s:157:"With this setting, you can define from when on info banner {$a->no} should be displayed. The configured time is interpreted as server time, not as user time.";s:20:"infobannerendsetting";s:29:"Info banner {$a->no} end time";s:25:"infobannerendsetting_desc";s:155:"With this setting, you can define until when info banner {$a->no} should be displayed. The configured time is interpreted as server time, not as user time.";s:8:"tilestab";s:19:"Advertisement tiles";s:19:"tilesgeneralheading";s:27:"Advertisement tiles general";s:18:"tilecolumnssetting";s:44:"Number of advertisement tile columns per row";s:23:"tilecolumnssetting_desc";s:266:"Here, you define the number of columns per row in the presented grid of advertisement tiles. Please note that this number of columns applies to desktop / larger screens. On smaller screens and mobile screens, the advertisement tile columns are automatically wrapped.";s:28:"tilefrontpagepositionsetting";s:48:"Position of the advertisement tiles on site home";s:33:"tilefrontpagepositionsetting_desc";s:364:"Advertisement tiles are shown on site home only. With this setting, you control if the advertisement tiles are displayed before the site home content or after the site home content. If you want to show only the advertisement tiles on site home and nothing else, all other site home content can be removed by changing the <a href="{$a->url}">site home settings</a>.";s:35:"tilefrontpagepositionsetting_before";s:28:"Before the site home content";s:34:"tilefrontpagepositionsetting_after";s:27:"After the site home content";s:17:"tileheightsetting";s:26:"Advertisement tiles height";s:22:"tileheightsetting_desc";s:254:"With this setting, you control the height of the advertisement tiles. The configured height is the minimum height of each tile. If a tile's content is higher than this configured height, the whole row of tiles will be automatically made higher as needed.";s:11:"tileheading";s:27:"Advertisement tile {$a->no}";s:34:"tilebackgroundimagepositionsetting";s:53:"Advertisement tile {$a->no} background image position";s:39:"tilebackgroundimagepositionsetting_desc";s:207:"With this setting, you control the positioning of the background image within the advertisement tile {$a->no} container. The first value is the horizontal position, the second value is the vertical position.";s:30:"tilebackgroundimagesizesetting";s:49:"Advertisement tile {$a->no} background image size";s:35:"tilebackgroundimagesizesetting_desc";s:387:"With this setting, you control how the background image of advertisement tile {$a->no} is scaled within the tile. Use 'Cover' to fully fill the tile (which may crop parts of the image), 'Contain' to show the whole image (without cropping but maybe with empty space), 'Auto' to use the image's intrinsic size, or a percentage value to scale the image proportionally to the tile container.";s:35:"tilebackgroundimagesizesetting_auto";s:4:"Auto";s:38:"tilebackgroundimagesizesetting_contain";s:7:"Contain";s:36:"tilebackgroundimagesizesetting_cover";s:5:"Cover";s:40:"tilebackgroundimagesizesetting_90percent";s:3:"90%";s:40:"tilebackgroundimagesizesetting_75percent";s:3:"75%";s:40:"tilebackgroundimagesizesetting_50percent";s:3:"50%";s:40:"tilebackgroundimagesizesetting_25percent";s:3:"25%";s:26:"tilebackgroundimagesetting";s:44:"Advertisement tile {$a->no} background image";s:31:"tilebackgroundimagesetting_desc";s:325:"Here, you can upload an image file which will be shown as background image behind the content of the advertisement tile {$a->no}. Please make sure or check that the content is still readable on the background image. This is an optional setting, the advertisement tile will work even if you do not upload any background image.";s:18:"tilecontentsetting";s:35:"Advertisement tile {$a->no} content";s:23:"tilecontentsetting_desc";s:243:"Here, you enter the content which should be displayed in the advertisement tile {$a->no}. The content is displayed in the middle of the tile. This is an optional setting, the advertisement tile will be shown even if you do not set any content.";s:23:"tilecontentstylesetting";s:41:"Advertisement tile {$a->no} content style";s:28:"tilecontentstylesetting_dark";s:51:"Dark (black font color for light background images)";s:34:"tilecontentstylesetting_darkshadow";s:80:"Dark & Shadow (black font color with a light shadow for light background images)";s:28:"tilecontentstylesetting_desc";s:307:"Here, you can modify the style of the content of advertisement tile {$a->no}. By default, the content style is controlled by the style which you set in the rich-text editor above. However, to allow consistent and easy styling especially when using text on background images, you can override the style here.";s:32:"tilecontentstylesetting_nochange";s:55:"No change (control all styling in the rich-text editor)";s:29:"tilecontentstylesetting_light";s:51:"Light (white font color for dark background images)";s:35:"tilecontentstylesetting_lightshadow";s:79:"Light & Shadow (white font color with a dark shadow for dark background images)";s:18:"tileenabledsetting";s:34:"Enable advertisement tile {$a->no}";s:23:"tileenabledsetting_desc";s:62:"With this setting, you can enable advertisement tile {$a->no}.";s:15:"tilelinksetting";s:36:"Advertisement tile {$a->no} link URL";s:20:"tilelinksetting_desc";s:236:"Here, you can set a (Moodle-internal or external) URL which will be offered as link button at the end of the advertisement tile {$a->no}. This is an optional setting, the advertisement tile will work even if you do not set any link URL.";s:21:"tilelinktitlefallback";s:4:"Link";s:20:"tilelinktitlesetting";s:38:"Advertisement tile {$a->no} link title";s:25:"tilelinktitlesetting_desc";s:256:"Here, you can set a link title which is used as label of the link button as soon as you set a link URL in the advertisement tile {$a->no}. Please note that if you set a link URL but do not set a link title, the link button will just be labeled with 'Link'.";s:21:"tilelinktargetsetting";s:39:"Advertisement tile {$a->no} link target";s:26:"tilelinktargetsetting_desc";s:132:"Here, you can set the link target which is set for the link button as soon as you set a link URL in the advertisement tile {$a->no}.";s:32:"tilelinktargetsetting_samewindow";s:11:"Same window";s:28:"tilelinktargetsetting_newtab";s:7:"New tab";s:16:"tileordersetting";s:42:"Advertisement tile {$a->no} order position";s:21:"tileordersetting_desc";s:438:"With this setting, you define the order position of the advertisement tile {$a->no}. By default, the advertisement tiles are ordered from top to bottom and left to right like you see them on this settings page here. However, you can decide to assign another order position with this setting. If you assign the same order position to two or more advertisement tiles, they will be ordered again according to the order on this settings page.";s:16:"tiletitlesetting";s:33:"Advertisement tile {$a->no} title";s:21:"tiletitlesetting_desc";s:185:"Here, you enter the title which should be displayed in the advertisement tile {$a->no}. This is an optional setting, the advertisement tile will be shown even if you do not set a title.";s:9:"slidertab";s:6:"Slider";s:20:"slidergeneralheading";s:14:"Slider general";s:22:"slideranimationsetting";s:21:"Slider animation type";s:27:"slideranimationsetting_desc";s:158:"With this setting, you control the slider animation. 'Slide' applies a sliding animation, 'Fade' applies a fading animation and 'None' removes all animations.";s:27:"slideranimationsetting_fade";s:4:"Fade";s:27:"slideranimationsetting_none";s:4:"None";s:28:"slideranimationsetting_slide";s:5:"Slide";s:21:"sliderarrownavsetting";s:23:"Enable arrow navigation";s:26:"sliderarrownavsetting_desc";s:77:"With this setting, you can add navigation arrows on both sides of the slider.";s:30:"sliderfrontpagepositionsetting";s:35:"Position of the slider on site home";s:35:"sliderfrontpagepositionsetting_desc";s:327:"The slider is shown on site home only. With this setting, you control if the slider is displayed before the site home content or after the site home content. If you want to show only the slider on site home and nothing else, all other site home content can be removed by changing the <a href="{$a->url}">site home settings</a>.";s:41:"sliderfrontpagepositionsetting_afterafter";s:63:"After the site home content (and after the advertisement tiles)";s:42:"sliderfrontpagepositionsetting_afterbefore";s:64:"After the site home content (but before the advertisement tiles)";s:42:"sliderfrontpagepositionsetting_beforeafter";s:64:"Before the site home content (but after the advertisement tiles)";s:43:"sliderfrontpagepositionsetting_beforebefore";s:65:"Before the site home content (and before the advertisement tiles)";s:25:"sliderindicatornavsetting";s:34:"Enable slider indicator navigation";s:30:"sliderindicatornavsetting_desc";s:81:"With this setting, you can add navigation indicators on the bottom of the slider.";s:21:"sliderintervalsetting";s:21:"Slider interval speed";s:26:"sliderintervalsetting_desc";s:161:"With this setting, you control how long a slide is displayed in milliseconds. The minimum value is 1000 (one second) and the maximum value is 10000 (10 seconds).";s:21:"sliderkeyboardsetting";s:33:"Allow slider keyboard interaction";s:26:"sliderkeyboardsetting_desc";s:135:"With this setting, you enable keyboard inputs (arrow keys) to control the slider. Please note that disabling this lowers accessibility.";s:18:"sliderpausesetting";s:25:"Pause slider on mouseover";s:23:"sliderpausesetting_desc";s:160:"With this setting, you prevent the slider from cycling through the slides when a user hovers over a slide. Please note that disabling this lowers accessibility.";s:17:"sliderridesetting";s:20:"Cycle through slides";s:22:"sliderridesetting_desc";s:340:"With this setting, you control the cycling behaviour of the slider. 'On page load' begins cycling through slides after the page has finished loading, 'After interaction' will start cycling after a user has interacted with the slider. 'Never' disables the automatic cycling of slides altogether, requiring user input to cycle through slides.";s:34:"sliderridesetting_afterinteraction";s:17:"After interaction";s:23:"sliderridesetting_never";s:5:"Never";s:28:"sliderridesetting_onpageload";s:12:"On page load";s:17:"sliderwrapsetting";s:33:"Continuously cycle through slides";s:22:"sliderwrapsetting_desc";s:135:"With this setting, you make the slider cycling through all slides. If you disable this, the slider will stop cycling at the last slide.";s:12:"slideheading";s:14:"Slide {$a->no}";s:30:"slidebackgroundimagealtsetting";s:45:"Slide {$a->no} background image alt attribute";s:35:"slidebackgroundimagealtsetting_desc";s:231:"Here, you can set an alt attribute for the image of slide {$a->no}. This is an optional setting, the slide will be shown even if you do not set an alt attribute. Please note that not providing an alt attribute lowers accessibility.";s:27:"slidebackgroundimagesetting";s:31:"Slide {$a->no} background image";s:32:"slidebackgroundimagesetting_desc";s:531:"Here, you can upload an image file which will be shown as background image behind the content of slide {$a->no}. Please make sure or check that the content is still readable on the background image. Please also try to make sure that the aspect ratio of all slides' background images is equal (as the background image aspect ratio controls the height of the slide and you might want to avoid flickering when the slides are changed). This is a mandatory setting, the slide will not be shown if you do not upload any background image.";s:19:"slidecaptionsetting";s:22:"Slide {$a->no} caption";s:24:"slidecaptionsetting_desc";s:219:"Here, you enter the caption which should be displayed in slide {$a->no}. The caption is displayed at the bottom center of the slide. This is an optional setting, the slide will be shown even if you do not set a caption.";s:19:"slidecontentsetting";s:22:"Slide {$a->no} content";s:24:"slidecontentsetting_desc";s:600:"Here, you enter the content which should be displayed in slide {$a->no}. The content is displayed at the bottom center of the slide. If a caption is set, the content is displayed below the caption. Please note that the rich-text editor produces left-aligned text by default, but you might want to change that to centered text for a nicer look. Please also refrain from adding too much content to the slide and please test your content on small devices as content which overflows the slide will simply be hidden. This is an optional setting, the slide will be shown even if you do not set any content.";s:24:"slidecontentstylesetting";s:28:"Slide {$a->no} content style";s:29:"slidecontentstylesetting_dark";s:51:"Dark (black font color for light background images)";s:35:"slidecontentstylesetting_darkshadow";s:80:"Dark & Shadow (black font color with a light shadow for light background images)";s:29:"slidecontentstylesetting_desc";s:375:"Here, you can modify the style of the content of slide {$a->no}. By default, the content style is a white font color for dark background images. However, to allow consistent and easy styling on all kinds of background images, you can override the style here. Please note that this setting will overrrule the font color which you set in the rich-text editor above in any case.";s:30:"slidecontentstylesetting_light";s:51:"Light (white font color for dark background images)";s:36:"slidecontentstylesetting_lightshadow";s:79:"Light & Shadow (white font color with a dark shadow for dark background images)";s:19:"slideenabledsetting";s:21:"Enable slide {$a->no}";s:24:"slideenabledsetting_desc";s:49:"With this setting, you can enable slide {$a->no}.";s:16:"slidelinksetting";s:23:"Slide {$a->no} link URL";s:21:"slidelinksetting_desc";s:197:"Here, you can set a (Moodle-internal or external) URL which the slide content of slide {$a->no} will link to. This is an optional setting, the slide will be shown even if you do not set a link URL.";s:21:"slidelinktitlesetting";s:25:"Slide {$a->no} link title";s:26:"slidelinktitlesetting_desc";s:265:"Here, you can set a link title which is presented as tooltip as soon as the user hovers over slide {$a->no}. This is an optional setting, the slide will be linked even if you do not set a link title. Please note that not providing a link title lowers accessibility.";s:22:"slidelinksourcesetting";s:26:"Slide {$a->no} link source";s:27:"slidelinksourcesetting_desc";s:223:"Here, you can control which elements of the slider link to the given link URL. You can choose between linking the background image only, linking the slide's text elements (caption and content) only or linking both of these.";s:27:"slidelinksourcesetting_both";s:34:"Background image and text elements";s:28:"slidelinksourcesetting_image";s:21:"Background image only";s:27:"slidelinksourcesetting_text";s:18:"Text elements only";s:22:"slidelinktargetsetting";s:26:"Slide {$a->no} link target";s:27:"slidelinktargetsetting_desc";s:118:"Here, you can set the link target which is set for the slide link as soon as you set a link URL in the slide {$a->no}.";s:33:"slidelinktargetsetting_samewindow";s:11:"Same window";s:29:"slidelinktargetsetting_newtab";s:7:"New tab";s:17:"slideordersetting";s:29:"Slide {$a->no} order position";s:22:"slideordersetting_desc";s:360:"With this setting, you define the order position of the slide {$a->no}. By default, the slides are ordered as you see them on this settings page here. However, you can decide to assign another order position with this setting. If you assign the same order position to two or more slides, they will be ordered again according to the order on this settings page.";s:24:"configtitlefunctionality";s:13:"Functionality";s:10:"coursestab";s:7:"Courses";s:36:"courserelatedhintsforteachersheading";s:33:"Course related hints for teachers";s:31:"showswitchedroleincoursesetting";s:27:"Show hint for switched role";s:36:"showswitchedroleincoursesetting_desc";s:327:"With this setting a hint will appear in the course header if the user has switched the role in the course. By default, this information is only displayed right near the user's avatar in the user menu. By enabling this option, you can show this information - together with a link to switch back - within the course page as well.";s:14:"switchedroleto";s:80:"You are viewing this course currently with the role: <strong>{$a->role}</strong>";s:27:"showhintcoursehiddensetting";s:27:"Show hint in hidden courses";s:32:"showhintcoursehiddensetting_desc";s:229:"With this setting a hint will appear in the course header as long as the visibility of the course is hidden. This helps to identify the visibility state of a course at a glance without the need for looking at the course settings.";s:27:"showhintcoursehiddengeneral";s:108:"This course is currently <strong>hidden</strong>. Only enrolled teachers can access this course when hidden.";s:32:"showhintcoursehiddensettingslink";s:77:"You can change the visibility in the <a href="{$a->url}">course settings</a>.";s:33:"showhintforumnotificationssetting";s:51:"Show hint for forum notifications in hidden courses";s:38:"showhintforumnotificationssetting_desc";s:269:"With this setting a hint will not only appear in the course header but also in forums as long as the visibility of the course is hidden. This is to clarify that notifications within a forum are not send to students and to help the teachers understand this circumstance.";s:26:"showhintforumnotifications";s:171:"This course is currently <strong>hidden</strong>. This means that <strong>students will not be notified</strong> online or by email of any messages you post in this forum.";s:30:"showhintcourseselfenrolsetting";s:50:"Show hint for self enrolment without enrolment key";s:35:"showhintcourseselfenrolsetting_desc";s:144:"With this setting a hint will appear in the course header if the course is visible and an enrolment without enrolment key is currently possible.";s:37:"showhintcourseselfenrolstartcurrently";s:118:"This course is currently visible to everyone and <strong>self enrolment without an enrolment key</strong> is possible.";s:34:"showhintcourseselfenrolstartfuture";s:136:"This course is currently visible to everyone and <strong>self enrolment without an enrolment key</strong> is planned to become possible.";s:32:"showhintcourseselfenrolunlimited";s:99:"The <strong>{$a->name}</strong> enrolment instance allows unrestricted self enrolment indefinitely.";s:28:"showhintcourseselfenroluntil";s:104:"The <strong>{$a->name}</strong> enrolment instance allows unrestricted self enrolment until {$a->until}.";s:27:"showhintcourseselfenrolfrom";s:105:"The <strong>{$a->name}</strong> enrolment instance allows unrestricted self enrolment from {$a->from} on.";s:28:"showhintcourseselfenrolsince";s:96:"The <strong>{$a->name}</strong> enrolment instance allows unrestricted self enrolment currently.";s:32:"showhintcourseselfenrolfromuntil";s:120:"The <strong>{$a->name}</strong> enrolment instance allows unrestricted self enrolment from {$a->from} until {$a->until}.";s:33:"showhintcourseselfenrolsinceuntil";s:104:"The <strong>{$a->name}</strong> enrolment instance allows unrestricted self enrolment until {$a->until}.";s:44:"showhintcourseselfenrolinstancecallforaction";s:116:"If you don't want any Moodle user to have access to this course freely, please restrict the self enrolment settings.";s:31:"showhintcourseguestenrolsetting";s:29:"Show hint for guest enrolment";s:36:"showhintcourseguestenrolsetting_desc";s:125:"With this setting a hint will appear in the course header if the course is visible and guest enrolment is currently possible.";s:36:"showhintcourseguestenrolsetting_note";s:182:"Note: If you want to enhance the hint with a link to the course of any kind, you have the {&dollar;a->courseid} placeholder available which can be used in the language customization.";s:47:"showhintcourseguestenrolsetting_withoutpassword";s:48:"Yes, but only if no guest access password is set";s:38:"showhintcourseguestenrolsetting_always";s:43:"Yes, even if a guest access password is set";s:28:"showhintcourseguestenrolhint";s:116:"This course is currently visible to everyone and <strong>guest access without a guest password</strong> is possible.";s:34:"showhintcourseguestenrolhintalways";s:90:"This course is currently visible to everyone and guest access with a password is possible.";s:32:"showhintcourseguestenrolauthonly";s:106:"All logged-in Moodle users can access the content of this course freely without enrolling into the course.";s:38:"showhintcourseguestenrolauthonlyalways";s:138:"All logged-in Moodle users can access the content of this course without enrolling into the course if they know the guest access password.";s:32:"showhintcourseguestenroleveryone";s:136:"All Moodle users and even users without a Moodle account can access the content of this course freely without enrolling into the course.";s:38:"showhintcourseguestenroleveryonealways";s:168:"All Moodle users and even users without a Moodle account can access the content of this course without enrolling into the course if they know the guest access password.";s:37:"showhintcourseguestenrolcallforaction";s:154:"If you don't want to grant free access to this course, please disable guest access or set a guest password in the <a href="{$a->url}">course settings</a>.";s:43:"showhintcourseguestenrolcallforactionalways";s:131:"If you don't want to grant guest access to this course, please disable guest access in the <a href="{$a->url}">course settings</a>.";s:36:"courserelatedhintsforstudentsheading";s:33:"Course related hints for students";s:31:"showhintcoursguestaccesssetting";s:26:"Show hint for guest access";s:37:"showhintcourseguestaccesssetting_desc";s:216:"With this setting a hint will appear in the course header when a user is accessing it with the guest access feature. If the course provides an active self enrolment, a link to that page is also presented to the user.";s:32:"showhintcourseguestaccessgeneral";s:69:"You are currently viewing this course as <strong>{$a->role}</strong>.";s:29:"showhintcourseguestaccesslink";s:95:"To have full access to the course, you can <a href="{$a->url}">self enrol into this course</a>.";s:24:"configtitleaccessibility";s:13:"Accessibility";s:17:"administrationtab";s:14:"Administration";s:23:"coursemanagementheading";s:17:"Course management";s:37:"showviewcourseiconincoursemgntsetting";s:21:"Show view course icon";s:44:"showviewcourseiconincoursemgntsesetting_desc";s:343:"By default, on the <a href="{$a}">course management page</a>, Moodle requires you to either open the course details or to pass through the course settings before you can click an additional UI element to view the course. By enabling this setting, you can add a 'View course' icon directly to the category listing on the course management page.";s:27:"accessibilitydeclarationtab";s:11:"Declaration";s:31:"accessibilitydeclarationheading";s:28:"Declaration of accessibility";s:37:"enableaccessibilitydeclarationsetting";s:40:"Enable declaration of accessibility page";s:42:"enableaccessibilitydeclarationsetting_desc";s:158:"With this setting, you can enable a declaration of accessibility page. It will behave just like the <a href="{$a->url}">other static pages</a> in Boost Union.";s:32:"accessibilitydeclarationdisabled";s:106:"The declaration of accessibility information page is disabled for this site. There is nothing to see here.";s:38:"accessibilitydeclarationcontentsetting";s:41:"Declaration of accessibility page content";s:43:"accessibilitydeclarationcontentsetting_desc";s:106:"In this setting, you can add rich text content which will be shown on a declaration of accessibility page.";s:40:"accessibilitydeclarationpagetitledefault";s:28:"Declaration of accessibility";s:40:"accessibilitydeclarationpagetitlesetting";s:39:"Declaration of accessibility page title";s:45:"accessibilitydeclarationpagetitlesetting_desc";s:248:"In this setting, you can define the title of the declaration of accessibility page. This text will be used as link text to the declaration of accessibility page as well if you configure 'Declaration of accessibility page link position' accordingly.";s:40:"accessibilitydeclarationlinkpositionnone";s:73:"Do not automatically show a link to the declaration of accessibility page";s:44:"accessibilitydeclarationlinkpositionfootnote";s:67:"Add a link to the declaration of accessibility page to the footnote";s:42:"accessibilitydeclarationlinkpositionfooter";s:85:"Add a link to the declaration of accessibility page to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:40:"accessibilitydeclarationlinkpositionboth";s:105:"Add a link to the declaration of accessibility page to the footnote and to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:43:"accessibilitydeclarationlinkpositionsetting";s:47:"Declaration of accessibility page link position";s:48:"accessibilitydeclarationlinkpositionsetting_desc";s:250:"In this setting, you can configure if a link to the declaration of accessibility page should be added automatically to the Moodle page. If you do not want to show a link automatically, you can add a link to {$a->url} from anywhere in Moodle manually.";s:23:"accessibilitysupporttab";s:12:"Support page";s:27:"accessibilitysupportheading";s:26:"Accessibility support page";s:26:"accessibilitysupportsubmit";s:6:"Submit";s:33:"enableaccessibilitysupportsetting";s:33:"Enable accessibility support page";s:38:"enableaccessibilitysupportsetting_desc";s:146:"With this setting, you can enable a accessibility support page. It will behave similar to <a href="{$a->url}">Moodle core's site support page</a>.";s:28:"accessibilitysupportdisabled";s:87:"The accessibility support page is disabled for this site. There is nothing to see here.";s:34:"accessibilitysupportdefaultsubject";s:22:"Accessibility feedback";s:35:"accessibilitysupportusermailsubject";s:29:"Accessibility support request";s:31:"accessibilitysupportmessagesent";s:44:"Your accessibility support request was sent.";s:34:"accessibilitysupportmessagenotsent";s:67:"Unfortunately your accessibility support request could not be sent.";s:35:"accessibilitysupportmessagetryagain";s:23:"Please try again later.";s:41:"accessibilitysupportmessagetryalternative";s:83:"Please try again later or sent an email directly to <a href="mailto:{$a}">{$a}</a>.";s:34:"accessibilitysupportcontentsetting";s:34:"Accessibility support page content";s:39:"accessibilitysupportcontentsetting_desc";s:192:"In this setting, you can add rich text content which will be shown on the accessibility support page, together with a form to send accessibility feedback or to report an accessibility barrier.";s:34:"accessibilitysupportcontentdefault";s:523:"<p>If you have any accessibility feedback or want to report a barrier, please use the form below.</p><p>Do you work with assistive technology such as screen readers, magnifiers, voice control or speech recognition software? If yes, please specify which ones. To help us to process your request, you can allow the form to automatically send the following information along with your message: The URL on which you were when you opened this support form (this is called 'referrer') and some information about your browser.</p>";s:36:"accessibilitysupportpagetitledefault";s:21:"Accessibility support";s:36:"accessibilitysupportpagetitlesetting";s:32:"Accessibility support page title";s:41:"accessibilitysupportpagetitlesetting_desc";s:239:"In this setting, you can define the title of the accessibility support page. This text will be used as link text to the accessibility support information page as well if you configure 'Accessibility support page link position' accordingly.";s:36:"accessibilitysupportlinkpositionnone";s:66:"Do not automatically show a link to the accessibility support page";s:40:"accessibilitysupportlinkpositionfootnote";s:60:"Add a link to the accessibility support page to the footnote";s:38:"accessibilitysupportlinkpositionfooter";s:78:"Add a link to the accessibility support page to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:36:"accessibilitysupportlinkpositionboth";s:98:"Add a link to the accessibility support page to the footnote and to the footer (questionmark) icon";s:39:"accessibilitysupportlinkpositionsetting";s:40:"Accessibility support page link position";s:44:"accessibilitysupportlinkpositionsetting_desc";s:243:"In this setting, you can configure if a link to the accessibility support page should be added automatically to the Moodle page. If you do not want to show a link automatically, you can add a link to {$a->url} from anywhere in Moodle manually.";s:37:"allowaccessibilitysupportwithoutlogin";s:46:"Allow accessibility support page without login";s:42:"allowaccessibilitysupportwithoutlogin_desc";s:212:"If this setting is enabled, the accessibility support page will be shown to users who are not logged in. If this setting is disabled, only logged in users will be allowed to access the accessibility support page.";s:45:"enableaccessibilitysupportfooterbuttonsetting";s:42:"Enable accessibility support footer button";s:50:"enableaccessibilitysupportfooterbuttonsetting_desc";s:142:"With this setting, you can add a link to the accessibility support page as a floating accessibility icon above the footer (questionmark) icon.";s:28:"allowanonymoussubmitssetting";s:40:"Allow anonymous support page submissions";s:33:"allowanonymoussubmitssetting_desc";s:251:"With this setting, you can allow the user to send the accessibility feedback anonymously through the accessibility support page. Users can then decide if they want to send feedback anonymously (without sending their username and email address) or not.";s:37:"accessibilitysupportanonymouscheckbox";s:61:"I prefer to send my accessibility support request anonymously";s:33:"accessibilitysupportanonymoususer";s:14:"Anonymous user";s:34:"accessibilitysupportanonymousemail";s:23:"anonymous@email.invalid";s:40:"accessibilitysupportsentforanonymoususer";s:67:"The user requested to send this accessibility feedback anonymously.";s:29:"allowsendtechinfoalongsetting";s:41:"Allow sending technical information along";s:34:"allowsendtechinfoalongsetting_desc";s:185:"With this setting, you can allow the user to send technical information along on the accessibility support page. Users can then decide if they want to send technical information or not.";s:36:"accessibilitysupporttechinfocheckbox";s:73:"I agree to send the following technical information along with my message";s:28:"accessibilitysupporttechinfo";s:21:"Technical information";s:33:"accessibilitysupporttechinfolabel";s:35:"Technical information to send along";s:36:"accessibilitysupporttechinforeferrer";s:13:"Referrer page";s:35:"accessibilitysupporttechinfosysinfo";s:18:"System information";s:28:"accessibilitysupportusermail";s:31:"Accessibility support user mail";s:33:"accessibilitysupportusermail_desc";s:214:"Here you define the email address to which the accessibility support requests should be sent. If you leave this field empty, the requests will be sent to the <a href="{$a->url}">configured site support contact</a>.";s:33:"accessibilitysupportuserfirstname";s:13:"Accessibility";s:32:"accessibilitysupportuserlastname";s:7:"support";s:42:"accessibilitysupportpagesrlinktitledefault";s:25:"Get accessibility support";s:42:"accessibilitysupportpagesrlinktitlesetting";s:50:"Accessibility support page screenreader link title";s:47:"accessibilitysupportpagesrlinktitlesetting_desc";s:169:"In this setting, you can define the screenreader link title for the accessibility support page. This text will be used as link text which is only shown to screenreaders.";s:29:"accessibilitysupportrecaptcha";s:44:"Add re-captcha to accessibility support page";s:34:"accessibilitysupportrecaptcha_desc";s:652:"With this setting, you control if a re-captcha is added to the accessibility support page. This is to prevent spam and abuse of the accessibility support form, just like it is done within <a href="{$a->support}">Moodle core's support form</a>. However, adding re-captchas add an additional accessibility barrier for users who use screenreaders or other assistive technologies which might be counter-productive in this case. Thus, please choose wisely if you want to enable this setting. Please also note that, even if enabled, the re-captcha is not shown until you set the necessary <a href="{$a->settings}">API keys in the authentication settings</a>.";s:19:"configtitleflavours";s:8:"Flavours";s:39:"flavoursactivityiconcoloradministration";s:40:"Activity icon color for "Administration"";s:44:"flavoursactivityiconcoloradministration_help";s:137:"With this setting, the flavour will override the activity icon "Administration" color which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:35:"flavoursactivityiconcolorassessment";s:36:"Activity icon color for "Assessment"";s:40:"flavoursactivityiconcolorassessment_help";s:133:"With this setting, the flavour will override the activity icon "Assessment" color which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:38:"flavoursactivityiconcolorcollaboration";s:39:"Activity icon color for "Collaboration"";s:43:"flavoursactivityiconcolorcollaboration_help";s:136:"With this setting, the flavour will override the activity icon "Collaboration" color which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:38:"flavoursactivityiconcolorcommunication";s:39:"Activity icon color for "Communication"";s:43:"flavoursactivityiconcolorcommunication_help";s:136:"With this setting, the flavour will override the activity icon "Communication" color which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:32:"flavoursactivityiconcolorcontent";s:33:"Activity icon color for "Content"";s:37:"flavoursactivityiconcolorcontent_help";s:130:"With this setting, the flavour will override the activity icon "Content" color which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:43:"flavoursactivityiconcolorinteractivecontent";s:45:"Activity icon color for "Interactive content"";s:48:"flavoursactivityiconcolorinteractivecontent_help";s:142:"With this setting, the flavour will override the activity icon "Interactive content" color which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:34:"flavoursactivityiconcolorinterface";s:35:"Activity icon color for "Interface"";s:39:"flavoursactivityiconcolorinterface_help";s:132:"With this setting, the flavour will override the activity icon "Interface" color which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:17:"flavoursappliesto";s:10:"Applies to";s:25:"flavoursapplytocategories";s:26:"Apply to course categories";s:30:"flavoursapplytocategories_help";s:72:"Here, you define if this flavour should be applied to course categories.";s:29:"flavoursapplytocategories_ids";s:17:"Course categories";s:34:"flavoursapplytocategories_ids_help";s:217:"Here, you define one or more particular course categories which this flavour should be applied to. As soon as the rendered Moodle page is located within one of the configured course categories, the flavour is applied.";s:22:"flavoursapplytocohorts";s:16:"Apply to cohorts";s:27:"flavoursapplytocohorts_help";s:62:"Here, you define if this flavour should be applied to cohorts.";s:26:"flavoursapplytocohorts_ids";s:7:"Cohorts";s:31:"flavoursapplytocohorts_ids_help";s:460:"Here, you define one or more particular cohorts which this flavour should be applied to. As soon as the user is a member of one of the configured cohorts, the flavour is applied.<br /><br />Please note that, if you define more than one cohorts, there is no need for the user to be a member of all of them at the same time.<br /><br />Please also note that at the current state of implementation category cohorts are treated just as if they were system cohorts.";s:23:"flavoursbackgroundimage";s:16:"Background image";s:28:"flavoursbackgroundimage_help";s:117:"With this setting, the flavour will override the background image which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:31:"flavoursbackgroundimageposition";s:25:"Background image position";s:36:"flavoursbackgroundimageposition_help";s:126:"With this setting, the flavour will override the background image position which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:22:"flavoursbacktooverview";s:24:"Back to flavour overview";s:28:"flavoursbootstrapcolordanger";s:28:"Bootstrap color for "Danger"";s:33:"flavoursbootstrapcolordanger_help";s:125:"With this setting, the flavour will override the Bootstrap "danger" color which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:26:"flavoursbootstrapcolorinfo";s:26:"Bootstrap color for "Info"";s:31:"flavoursbootstrapcolorinfo_help";s:123:"With this setting, the flavour will override the Bootstrap info "color" which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:29:"flavoursbootstrapcolorsuccess";s:29:"Bootstrap color for "Success"";s:34:"flavoursbootstrapcolorsuccess_help";s:126:"With this setting, the flavour will override the Bootstrap "success" color which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:29:"flavoursbootstrapcolorwarning";s:29:"Bootstrap color for "Warning"";s:34:"flavoursbootstrapcolorwarning_help";s:126:"With this setting, the flavour will override the Bootstrap "warning" color which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:18:"flavoursbrandcolor";s:19:"Primary brand color";s:23:"flavoursbrandcolor_help";s:120:"With this setting, the flavour will override the primary brand color which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:17:"flavourslinkcolor";s:16:"Link brand color";s:22:"flavourslinkcolor_help";s:111:"With this setting, the flavour will override the link color which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:24:"flavoursbuttonbrandcolor";s:18:"Button brand color";s:29:"flavoursbuttonbrandcolor_help";s:119:"With this setting, the flavour will override the button brand color which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:24:"flavoursbrandedgraytones";s:22:"Use branded gray tones";s:29:"flavoursbrandedgraytones_help";s:127:"With this setting, the flavour will override the branded gray tones setting which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:21:"flavourscreateflavour";s:14:"Create flavour";s:18:"flavourscustomscss";s:8:"Raw SCSS";s:23:"flavourscustomscss_help";s:170:"With this setting, you can write custom SCSS for the flavour. It will be appended to the stack of CSS code which is shipped to the browser as soon as the flavour applies.";s:21:"flavourscustomscsspre";s:16:"Raw initial SCSS";s:26:"flavourscustomscsspre_help";s:176:"With this setting, you can write custom initial SCSS for the flavour. It will be used when building the CSS code which is shipped to the browser as soon as the flavour applies.";s:14:"flavoursdelete";s:6:"Delete";s:21:"flavoursdeleteflavour";s:14:"Delete flavour";s:26:"flavoursdeleteconfirmation";s:55:"Do you really want to delete the flavour <em>{$a}</em>?";s:19:"flavoursdescription";s:11:"Description";s:24:"flavoursdescription_help";s:120:"The flavour's description is just used internally to allow you to identify a particular flavour in the list of flavours.";s:12:"flavoursedit";s:4:"Edit";s:19:"flavourseditflavour";s:12:"Edit flavour";s:15:"flavoursfavicon";s:7:"Favicon";s:20:"flavoursfavicon_help";s:108:"With this setting, the flavour will override the favicon which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:16:"flavoursfootnote";s:8:"Footnote";s:21:"flavoursfootnote_help";s:112:"With this setting, the flavour will override the footnote which is configured in Boost Union's content settings.";s:16:"flavoursflavours";s:8:"Flavours";s:23:"flavoursgeneralsettings";s:16:"General settings";s:28:"flavoursincludesubcategories";s:21:"Include subcategories";s:33:"flavoursincludesubcategories_help";s:91:"If checked, the flavour will also be applied to the subcategories of the chosen categories.";s:12:"flavourslogo";s:4:"Logo";s:17:"flavourslogo_help";s:105:"With this setting, the flavour will override the logo which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:19:"flavourslogocompact";s:12:"Compact logo";s:24:"flavourslogocompact_help";s:105:"With this setting, the flavour will override the logo which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:19:"flavoursnavbarcolor";s:12:"Navbar color";s:24:"flavoursnavbarcolor_help";s:113:"With this setting, the flavour will override the navbar color which is configured in Boost Union's look settings.";s:18:"flavoursnavbartint";s:11:"Navbar tint";s:23:"flavoursnavbartint_help";s:216:"With this setting, the flavour will override the navbar tint color which is configured in Boost Union's look settings. This setting is only effective if the navbar color is set to one of the 'Colored navbar' options.";s:27:"flavoursnotificationcreated";s:36:"The flavour was created successfully";s:27:"flavoursnotificationdeleted";s:36:"The flavour was deleted successfully";s:26:"flavoursnotificationedited";s:35:"The flavour was edited successfully";s:24:"flavoursnothingtodisplay";s:92:"There aren't any flavours created yet. Please create your first flavour to get things going.";s:21:"flavoursoverview_desc";s:793:"<p>Boost Union's flavours offer a possibility to override particular Moodle look & feel settings in particular contexts. On this page, you can create and manage flavours.</p><p>Within each flavour, you define if it should be applied to particular course categories or particular cohorts. Afterwards, during each Moodle page rendering, Boost Union checks if any flavour applies. Please note that, for each Moodle page rendering, only the first matching flavour in the list is applied and the remaining flavours are ignored. Thus, the order of the flavours on this page is key.</p><p>Please note as well that after each change which you make to the set of flavours, the theme cache is purged. This is necessary to make sure that all assets are shipped properly and up-to-date to the browser.</p>";s:15:"flavourspreview";s:7:"Preview";s:22:"flavourspreviewflavour";s:15:"Preview flavour";s:24:"flavourspreviewblindtext";s:614:"Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Nunc id cursus metus aliquam eleifend mi in nulla. Felis imperdiet proin fermentum leo vel orci porta. Sed nisi lacus sed viverra tellus in hac habitasse. Vivamus arcu felis bibendum ut. Nisi porta lorem mollis aliquam ut porttitor. Odio euismod lacinia at quis risus sed vulputate odio. Sed felis eget velit aliquet sagittis id consectetur purus. Nec ullamcorper sit amet risus nullam eget. Pellentesque sit amet porttitor eget dolor. Cursus mattis molestie a iaculis at erat pellentesque.";s:13:"flavourstitle";s:5:"Title";s:18:"flavourstitle_help";s:114:"The flavour's title is just used internally to allow you to document a particular flavour in the list of flavours.";s:19:"configtitlesnippets";s:13:"SCSS snippets";s:19:"snippetsshowthecode";s:18:"Show the SCSS code";s:15:"snippetscreator";s:7:"Creator";s:19:"snippetsdescription";s:11:"Description";s:15:"snippetsdetails";s:7:"Details";s:22:"snippetsdetailspreview";s:7:"Preview";s:15:"snippetsdisable";s:7:"Disable";s:14:"snippetsenable";s:6:"Enable";s:12:"snippetsgoal";s:4:"Goal";s:25:"snippetsgoalaccessibility";s:13:"Accessibility";s:18:"snippetsgoalbugfix";s:6:"Bugfix";s:20:"snippetsgoaldevsonly";s:19:"For developers only";s:21:"snippetsgoaleaseofuse";s:11:"Ease of use";s:20:"snippetsgoaleyecandy";s:9:"Eye candy";s:24:"snippetsnothingtodisplay";s:151:"There aren't any SCSS snippets which can be used. Please go to the settings tab and enable the built-in SCSS snippets or upload your own SCSS snippets.";s:16:"snippetsoverview";s:8:"Overview";s:21:"snippetsoverview_desc";s:241:"Boost Union's SCSS snippets offer a possibility to add small (or slightly larger) amounts of SCSS to the Moodle site. This can be particularly handy for fixing small visual glitches in Moodle core or for adding eye candy to your Moodle site.";s:22:"snippetsoverview_notes";s:71:"To allow you to use SCSS snippets, please read these basic intructions:";s:23:"snippetsoverview_notes1";s:191:"SCSS snippets can come from multiple sources. You enable and configure each source on the 'Settings' tab. As soon as you have enabled at least one source, you will see the snippets list here.";s:23:"snippetsoverview_notes2";s:113:"SCSS snippets are added to the SCSS stack one after another. Thus, the order of the snippets on this page is key.";s:23:"snippetsoverview_notes3";s:207:"After each change which you make on this page, the theme cache is purged. This is necessary to make sure that the compiled SCSS code which is shipped to the browser is up-to-date and might take some seconds.";s:13:"snippetsscope";s:5:"Scope";s:19:"snippetsscopecourse";s:6:"Course";s:22:"snippetsscopedashboard";s:9:"Dashboard";s:21:"snippetsscopesitehome";s:9:"Site home";s:19:"snippetsscopeglobal";s:6:"Global";s:19:"snippetsshowdetails";s:12:"Show details";s:16:"snippetssnippets";s:13:"SCSS snippets";s:14:"snippetssource";s:6:"Source";s:31:"snippetssourcetheme_boost_union";s:20:"Boost Union built-in";s:22:"snippetssourceuploaded";s:6:"Upload";s:16:"snippetstestedon";s:9:"Tested on";s:13:"snippetstitle";s:5:"Title";s:20:"snippetstrackerissue";s:13:"Tracker issue";s:17:"snippetsusagenote";s:10:"Usage note";s:16:"snippetssettings";s:8:"Settings";s:30:"snippetsbuiltinsnippetsheading";s:17:"Built-in snippets";s:21:"enablebuiltinsnippets";s:24:"Enable built-in snippets";s:26:"enablebuiltinsnippets_desc";s:223:"With this setting, you can enable or disable the built-in SCSS snippets which are shipped with the Boost Union codebase. If you disable this setting, all built-in SCSS snippets are ignored and never added to the SCSS stack.";s:31:"snippetsuploadedsnippetsheading";s:17:"Uploaded snippets";s:36:"snippetsuploadedsnippetsheading_desc";s:395:"In addition to the built-in SCSS snippets which are officially maintained by the Boost Union team, there is the <a href="{$a}" target="_blank">SCSS snippets repository on Github</a> which is meant as a community hub for Boost Union SCSS snippets. Please find the instructions for using community SCSS snippets as well as the boilerplate to create your own local SCSS snippets in that repository.";s:22:"enableuploadedsnippets";s:24:"Enable uploaded snippets";s:27:"enableuploadedsnippets_desc";s:267:"With this setting, you can enable or disable uploading of SCSS snippets here within the Boost Union settings. If you disable this setting, uploading SCSS snippets is not possible and all previously uploaded SCSS snippets are ignored and never added to the SCSS stack.";s:16:"uploadedsnippets";s:15:"Upload snippets";s:21:"uploadedsnippets_desc";s:249:"You can either upload individual SCSS snippet files or a ZIP archive containing multiple SCSS snippet files – the ZIP file will be automatically extracted and the contained SCSS snippets will then be avaiable in this file area as individual files.";s:10:"smartmenus";s:11:"Smart menus";s:32:"error:smartmenusmenuitemnotfound";s:25:"Smart menu item not found";s:28:"error:smartmenusmenunotfound";s:20:"Smart menu not found";s:15:"smartmenus_desc";s:596:"<p>Smart menus allow site administrators to create customizable menus that can be placed in different locations on the site, such as the site main menu, bottom mobile menu, and user menu. The menus can be configured to display different types of content, including links to other pages or resources, category links, or user profile links.</p><p>Site administrators can create a new menu and specify the menu items, and display settings. The administrator can also choose where the menu will be displayed on the site and whether it should be visible to all users or only to certain user roles.</p>";s:18:"smartmenusbycohort";s:9:"By cohort";s:23:"smartmenusbycohort_help";s:52:"Restrict the visibility based on the user's cohorts.";s:16:"smartmenusbydate";s:7:"By date";s:20:"smartmenusbydatefrom";s:4:"From";s:25:"smartmenusbydatefrom_help";s:56:"Restrict the visibility before the given date is reached";s:21:"smartmenusbydateuntil";s:5:"Until";s:26:"smartmenusbydateuntil_help";s:55:"Restrict the visibility after the given date is reached";s:20:"smartmenusbylanguage";s:11:"By language";s:25:"smartmenusbylanguage_help";s:52:"Restrict the visibility based on the user's language";s:16:"smartmenusbyrole";s:7:"By role";s:21:"smartmenusbyrole_help";s:50:"Restrict the visibility based on the user's roles.";s:17:"smartmenusbyadmin";s:7:"Show to";s:22:"smartmenusbyadmin_help";s:77:"Restrict the visibility based on the fact if the user is a site admin or not.";s:21:"smartmenusbyadmin_all";s:9:"All users";s:24:"smartmenusbyadmin_admins";s:16:"Site admins only";s:27:"smartmenusbyadmin_nonadmins";s:15:"Non-admins only";s:40:"smartmenusdynamiccoursescompletionstatus";s:17:"Completion status";s:45:"smartmenusdynamiccoursescompletionstatus_help";s:290:"The dynamic courses menu item list will contain all courses of the user which match the selected completion status. For example, if you select 'In progress' as the completion status, the dynamic courses menu item list will only contain courses that the current user is currently working on.";s:49:"smartmenusdynamiccoursescompletionstatuscompleted";s:9:"Completed";s:48:"smartmenusdynamiccoursescompletionstatusenrolled";s:8:"Enrolled";s:50:"smartmenusdynamiccoursescompletionstatusinprogress";s:11:"In progress";s:38:"smartmenusdynamiccoursescoursecategory";s:15:"Course category";s:43:"smartmenusdynamiccoursescoursecategory_help";s:96:"The dynamic courses menu item list will contain all courses from the selected course categories.";s:45:"smartmenusdynamiccoursescoursecategorysubcats";s:21:"Include subcategories";s:50:"smartmenusdynamiccoursescoursecategorysubcats_help";s:125:"If checked, the dynamic courses menu will also contain all courses from the subcategories of the selected courses categories.";s:33:"smartmenusdynamiccoursesdaterange";s:10:"Date range";s:38:"smartmenusdynamiccoursesdaterange_help";s:100:"The dynamic courses menu item list will contain all courses which fall into the selected date range.";s:39:"smartmenusdynamiccoursesdaterangefuture";s:6:"Future";s:37:"smartmenusdynamiccoursesdaterangepast";s:4:"Past";s:40:"smartmenusdynamiccoursesdaterangepresent";s:7:"Present";s:37:"smartmenusdynamiccoursesenrolmentrole";s:14:"Enrolment role";s:42:"smartmenusdynamiccoursesenrolmentrole_help";s:110:"The dynamic courses menu item list will contain all courses where the user is enrolled with the selected role.";s:22:"smartmenusexperimental";s:535:"Please note: The smart menus functionality is fully usable in the current state of implementation, but has to be <em>considered as experimental</em> due to the large amount of setting combinations which still might trigger unexpected issues. Against this background, please test your smart menus with your individual menu settings thoroughly. If you encounter any issues with smart menus, please report them on <a href="https://github.com/moodle-an-hochschulen/moodle-theme_boost_union/issues">Github</a> with clear steps to reproduce.";s:30:"smartmenusgeneralsectionheader";s:16:"General settings";s:24:"smartmenusmenuaddnewitem";s:13:"Add menu item";s:22:"smartmenusmenucardform";s:9:"Card form";s:27:"smartmenusmenucardform_help";s:108:"Select the form of the card for card-style menus, choosing between square, portrait, landscape or fullwidth.";s:31:"smartmenusmenucardformfullwidth";s:10:"Full width";s:31:"smartmenusmenucardformlandscape";s:9:"Landscape";s:30:"smartmenusmenucardformportrait";s:8:"Portrait";s:28:"smartmenusmenucardformsquare";s:6:"Square";s:34:"smartmenusmenucardoverflowbehavior";s:22:"Card overflow behavior";s:39:"smartmenusmenucardoverflowbehavior_help";s:138:"Select how the menu should behave when it overflows its container, choosing between showing a scrollbar or wrapping the overflowing items.";s:40:"smartmenusmenucardoverflowbehaviornowrap";s:7:"No wrap";s:38:"smartmenusmenucardoverflowbehaviorwrap";s:4:"Wrap";s:22:"smartmenusmenucardsize";s:9:"Card size";s:27:"smartmenusmenucardsize_help";s:97:"Select the size of the card for card-style menus, choosing between tiny, small, medium, or large.";s:27:"smartmenusmenucardsizelarge";s:5:"Large";s:28:"smartmenusmenucardsizemedium";s:6:"Medium";s:27:"smartmenusmenucardsizesmall";s:5:"Small";s:26:"smartmenusmenucardsizetiny";s:4:"Tiny";s:20:"smartmenusmenucreate";s:11:"Create menu";s:27:"smartmenusmenucreatesuccess";s:31:"Smart menu created successfully";s:22:"smartmenusmenucssclass";s:9:"CSS class";s:27:"smartmenusmenucssclass_help";s:85:"Enter a CSS class for the menu. This can be used to apply custom styling to the menu.";s:27:"smartmenusmenudeleteconfirm";s:63:"Are you sure you want to delete this menu from the smart menus?";s:27:"smartmenusmenudeletesuccess";s:31:"Smart menu deleted successfully";s:25:"smartmenusmenudescription";s:11:"Description";s:30:"smartmenusmenudescription_help";s:164:"The description of the menu. This will be primarily used as internal documentation, but you can also show it within the menu by using the 'Show description' option.";s:23:"smartmenusmenuduplicate";s:28:"Duplicate menu and its items";s:30:"smartmenusmenuduplicatesuccess";s:47:"Menu and its menu items duplicated successfully";s:18:"smartmenusmenuedit";s:9:"Edit menu";s:25:"smartmenusmenueditsuccess";s:31:"Smart menu updated successfully";s:38:"smartmenusmenuitemcardappearanceheader";s:15:"Card appearance";s:37:"smartmenusmenuitemcardbackgroundcolor";s:21:"Card background color";s:42:"smartmenusmenuitemcardbackgroundcolor_help";s:57:"Select the background color for the card of the menu item";s:27:"smartmenusmenuitemcardimage";s:10:"Card image";s:32:"smartmenusmenuitemcardimage_help";s:67:"Select an image to display next to the menu item title in the card.";s:30:"smartmenusmenuitemcardimagealt";s:19:"Card image alt text";s:35:"smartmenusmenuitemcardimagealt_help";s:256:"The alt text for the card image of this menu item. You can use the placeholder {menutitle} to insert the configured menu item title into your own alt text. If you leave this field completely empty, the menu item text will be used automatically as alt text.";s:31:"smartmenusmenuitemcardtextcolor";s:15:"Card text color";s:36:"smartmenusmenuitemcardtextcolor_help";s:47:"Select the color for the card of the menu item.";s:24:"smartmenusmenuitemcreate";s:16:"Create menu item";s:31:"smartmenusmenuitemcreatesuccess";s:36:"Smart menu item created successfully";s:26:"smartmenusmenuitemcssclass";s:9:"CSS class";s:31:"smartmenusmenuitemcssclass_help";s:95:"Enter a CSS class for the menu item. This can be used to apply custom styling to the menu item.";s:31:"smartmenusmenuitemdeleteconfirm";s:67:"Are you sure you want to delete this menu item from the smart menu?";s:31:"smartmenusmenuitemdeletesuccess";s:36:"Smart menu item deleted successfully";s:35:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayallcourses";s:19:"Show hidden courses";s:23:"smartmenusmenuitememail";s:2:"To";s:28:"smartmenusmenuitememail_help";s:132:"Primary recipient email address(es) for the mailto link. Separate multiple addresses with commas. Do not include a 'mailto:' prefix.";s:32:"smartmenusmenuitememail_required";s:81:"Required – Enter at least one valid email address without the 'mailto:' prefix.";s:31:"smartmenusmenuitememail_invalid";s:84:"Please enter only valid email address(es), separated by commas if there are several.";s:26:"smartmenusmenuitememail_cc";s:2:"Cc";s:31:"smartmenusmenuitememail_cc_help";s:125:"Optional carbon-copy address(es), separate multiple addresses with commas. These are added to the mailto link as a Cc header.";s:27:"smartmenusmenuitememail_bcc";s:3:"Bcc";s:32:"smartmenusmenuitememail_bcc_help";s:132:"Optional blind carbon-copy address(es), separate multiple addresses with commas. These are added to the mailto link as a Bcc header.";s:31:"smartmenusmenuitememail_subject";s:7:"Subject";s:36:"smartmenusmenuitememail_subject_help";s:93:"Optional default subject line for the composed message. It is URL-encoded in the mailto link.";s:28:"smartmenusmenuitememail_body";s:12:"Message body";s:33:"smartmenusmenuitememail_body_help";s:92:"Optional default message body. It is URL-encoded in the mailto link (including line breaks).";s:35:"smartmenusmenuitemhidehiddencourses";s:19:"Hide hidden courses";s:43:"smartmenusmenuitemhiddencoursessorting_help";s:96:"Choose how hidden courses should be sorted in the course list of the dynamic courses menu items.";s:38:"smartmenusmenuitemhiddencoursessorting";s:22:"Hidden courses sorting";s:40:"smartmenusmenuitemhiddencoursesortingend";s:49:"Show hidden courses at the end of the course list";s:45:"smartmenusmenuitemhiddencoursesortingtogether";s:40:"Sort hidden and visible courses together";s:26:"smartmenusmenuitemlistsort";s:19:"Course list sorting";s:31:"smartmenusmenuitemlistsort_help";s:207:"The course list will be sorted by the selected criteria and sort order. Choose between fullname, shortname, course ID and course ID number as criteria in combination with ascending and descending sort order.";s:37:"smartmenusmenuitemlistsortfullnameasc";s:25:"Course fullname ascending";s:38:"smartmenusmenuitemlistsortfullnamedesc";s:26:"Course fullname descending";s:38:"smartmenusmenuitemlistsortshortnameasc";s:26:"Course shortname ascending";s:39:"smartmenusmenuitemlistsortshortnamedesc";s:27:"Course shortname descending";s:37:"smartmenusmenuitemlistsortcourseidasc";s:19:"Course ID ascending";s:38:"smartmenusmenuitemlistsortcourseiddesc";s:20:"Course ID descending";s:43:"smartmenusmenuitemlistsortcourseidnumberasc";s:26:"Course ID number ascending";s:44:"smartmenusmenuitemlistsortcourseidnumberdesc";s:27:"Course ID number descending";s:30:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayfield";s:35:"Course name presentation (1st line)";s:35:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayfield_help";s:276:"The course name which will be used as the title of the dynamic courses menu items. Choose between course full name, course short name, a custom course field or a combination of these. If you choose custom course field, you have to select the specific field to display as well.";s:44:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayfieldcoursefullname";s:16:"Course full name";s:45:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayfieldcourseshortname";s:17:"Course short name";s:41:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayfieldcustomfield";s:19:"Custom course field";s:49:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayfieldfullnamecustomfield";s:38:"Course full name (Custom course field)";s:47:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayfieldfullnameshortname";s:36:"Course full name (Course short name)";s:50:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayfieldshortnamecustomfield";s:39:"Course short name (Custom course field)";s:47:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayfieldshortnamefullname";s:36:"Course short name (Course full name)";s:36:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayfieldsecond";s:35:"Course name presentation (2nd line)";s:41:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayfieldsecond_help";s:313:"A second line which will be presented below the course name of a dynamic courses menu item. The second line is displayed in a smaller font size. Choose between course full name, course short name, or custom course field. If you choose custom course field, you have to select the specific field to display as well.";s:40:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayfieldsecondnone";s:20:"-- No second line --";s:46:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayfieldcustomfieldfirst";s:30:"Custom course field (1st line)";s:51:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayfieldcustomfieldfirst_help";s:135:"Select the custom course field which should be displayed as part of the course name in the first line of the dynamic courses menu item.";s:47:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayfieldcustomfieldsecond";s:30:"Custom course field (2nd line)";s:52:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayfieldcustomfieldsecond_help";s:136:"Select the custom course field which should be displayed as part of the course name in the second line of the dynamic courses menu item.";s:32:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayoptions";s:18:"Title presentation";s:37:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayoptions_help";s:56:"Choose how you want the menu item title to be displayed.";s:41:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayoptionshidetitle";s:51:"Hide title text and show only icon (on all devices)";s:47:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayoptionshidetitlemobile";s:54:"Hide title text and show only icon (on mobile devices)";s:45:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayoptionsshowtitleicon";s:27:"Show text and icon as title";s:43:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayonlyvisiblecourses";s:22:"Hidden courses display";s:48:"smartmenusmenuitemdisplayonlyvisiblecourses_help";s:180:"If enabled, the course list will not show hidden courses in any smart menu, even for administrators and users that have the capability moodle/course:viewhiddencourses in the course";s:27:"smartmenusmenuitemduplicate";s:19:"Duplicate menu item";s:34:"smartmenusmenuitemduplicatesuccess";s:33:"Menu item duplicated successfully";s:22:"smartmenusmenuitemedit";s:14:"Edit menu item";s:29:"smartmenusmenuitemeditsuccess";s:36:"Smart menu item updated successfully";s:22:"smartmenusmenuitemicon";s:4:"Icon";s:27:"smartmenusmenuitemicon_help";s:944:"The icon to display next to the menu item title.<br /><br />You can either select an icon from the Moodle core icon library, or use a FontAwesome icon. This is an important difference:<ul><li>Moodle core icons:<br />Moodle core defines its icons as "pix icons" and maps FontAwesome icons to these pix icons. The particular FontAwesome icon which is mapped is not guaranteed to be stable forever and might change in future Moodle core versions. Additionally, there are Moodle core pix icons which come with an additional Bootstrap color added to the icon.</li><li>FontAwesome icons:<br />FontAwesome icons are used as-is and their presentation will remain stable in future Moodle releases. It may just happen that the FontAwesome glyph may change if Moodle core upgrades to a future FontAwesome release.</li></ul>If you are in doubt and do not need to stick to a particular Moodle core pix icon, you should prefer to use a FontAwesome icon here.";s:34:"smartmenusmenuitemicon_placeholder";s:9:"Pick icon";s:29:"smartmenusmenuitemicon_noicon";s:16:"No icon selected";s:33:"smartmenusmenuitemicon_sourcecore";s:11:"Moodle core";s:36:"smartmenusmenuitemicon_sourcefablank";s:22:"FontAwesome Blank icon";s:36:"smartmenusmenuitemicon_sourcefasolid";s:17:"FontAwesome Solid";s:36:"smartmenusmenuitemicon_sourcefabrand";s:18:"FontAwesome Brands";s:39:"smartmenusmenuitemicon_ajaxtoomanyicons";s:60:"Too many icons ({$a}) to display. Please narrow your search.";s:28:"smartmenusmenuitemlinktarget";s:11:"Link target";s:33:"smartmenusmenuitemlinktarget_help";s:141:"The target for the link of the menu item. The menu item link will open in this target when clicked (i.e. in the same window or in a new tab).";s:34:"smartmenusmenuitemlinktargetnewtab";s:7:"New tab";s:38:"smartmenusmenuitemlinktargetsamewindow";s:11:"Same window";s:22:"smartmenusmenuitemmode";s:14:"Menu item mode";s:27:"smartmenusmenuitemmode_help";s:570:"<p>Select the mode how the menu item should be displayed within the menu.</p><ul><li>Inline: The menu item is displayed as a regular menu item within the menu. This is the default option.</li><li>Submenu: The menu item is displayed as a submenu item, which can be expanded or collapsed by clicking on the parent item. This mode is useful for building a third navigation level as well as for dynamic courses menu items, where course lists can be displayed as submenu items of this menu item. The title of this menu item is used as the text for the submenu item.</li></ul>";s:34:"smartmenusmenuitemnothingtodisplay";s:85:"There aren't any items added to this smart menu yet. Please add an item to this menu.";s:23:"smartmenusmenuitemorder";s:5:"Order";s:28:"smartmenusmenuitemorder_help";s:105:"Rearrange the position of item if needed. All menu items in the menu will be ordered by this order value.";s:36:"smartmenusmenuitempresentationheader";s:22:"Menu item presentation";s:28:"smartmenusmenuitemresponsive";s:17:"Responsive hiding";s:33:"smartmenusmenuitemresponsive_help";s:105:"By enabling any of these checkboxes, the menu item will be hidden on devices with the given display size.";s:35:"smartmenusmenuitemresponsivedesktop";s:7:"Desktop";s:34:"smartmenusmenuitemresponsivemobile";s:6:"Mobile";s:34:"smartmenusmenuitemresponsivetablet";s:6:"Tablet";s:29:"smartmenusmenuitemrestriction";s:12:"Access rules";s:19:"smartmenusmenuitems";s:10:"Menu items";s:33:"smartmenusmenuitemstructureheader";s:19:"Menu item structure";s:27:"smartmenusmenuitemtextcount";s:47:"Number of words for course full name (1st line)";s:32:"smartmenusmenuitemtextcount_help";s:198:"Specify the maximum number of words to be displayed from the course full name in the dynamic courses menu items. If you leave this field empty, the course full name will be displayed in full length.";s:33:"smartmenusmenuitemtextcountsecond";s:47:"Number of words for course full name (2nd line)";s:30:"smartmenusmenuitemtextposition";s:18:"Card text position";s:35:"smartmenusmenuitemtextposition_help";s:415:"<p>Select the position of the menu item text in relation to the card image, choosing from below image, top overlay and bottom overlay.</p><ul><li>Top overlay: Displays the menu item title over the overlay and at the top of the card.</li><li>Bottom overlay: Displays the menu item title over the overlay and at the bottom of the card.</li><li>Below image: Displays the menu item title below the card image.</li></ul>";s:40:"smartmenusmenuitemtextpositionbelowimage";s:11:"Below image";s:43:"smartmenusmenuitemtextpositionoverlaybottom";s:14:"Bottom overlay";s:40:"smartmenusmenuitemtextpositionoverlaytop";s:11:"Top overlay";s:23:"smartmenusmenuitemtitle";s:5:"Title";s:28:"smartmenusmenuitemtitle_help";s:72:"The title of the menu. This will be used as the label of this menu item.";s:25:"smartmenusmenuitemtooltip";s:7:"Tooltip";s:30:"smartmenusmenuitemtooltip_help";s:76:"The tooltip which will be displayed when the user hovers over the menu item.";s:22:"smartmenusmenuitemtype";s:14:"Menu item type";s:27:"smartmenusmenuitemtype_help";s:1275:"<p>Select the type of menu item you want to create, choosing between static, mailto, heading, moodle documentation, dynamic courses, and divider.</p><ul><li>Static: A static menu item is simply a link to a fixed URL that does not change.</li><li>Mailto: A mailto menu item opens the user's default email client to compose a message. You can set To, optional Cc and Bcc, and optional subject and message body; each address field can list multiple addresses separated by commas.</li><li>Heading: A heading menu item is used to group related menu items together under a common heading. It does not have a link and is not clickable.</li><li>Separator: A dividerenu item displays a horizontal line in the menu to visually separate groups of menu items.</li><li>Moodle documentation: A moodle documenation menu item is used to link to the corresponding MoodleDocs article, similar to the MoodleDocs link which is located in the Moodle footer (questionmark icon).</li><li>Dynamic courses: A dynamic courses menu item is used to display a list of courses based on certain criteria, such as course category, course enrolment role, course completion status or date range. The content displayed in a dynamic courses menu item will update automatically as the criteria changes.</li></ul>";s:26:"smartmenusmenuitemtypedocs";s:20:"Moodle documentation";s:36:"smartmenusmenuitemtypedynamiccourses";s:15:"Dynamic courses";s:29:"smartmenusmenuitemtypeheading";s:7:"Heading";s:29:"smartmenusmenuitemtypedivider";s:7:"Divider";s:28:"smartmenusmenuitemtypemailto";s:6:"Mailto";s:28:"smartmenusmenuitemtypestatic";s:6:"Static";s:21:"smartmenusmenuitemurl";s:13:"Menu item URL";s:26:"smartmenusmenuitemurl_help";s:103:"The static URL for the menu item. This is the link that will be followed when the menu item is clicked.";s:22:"smartmenusmenulocation";s:16:"Menu location(s)";s:27:"smartmenusmenulocation_help";s:807:"<p>Select the location(s) where you want the menu to appear on the page:</p><ul><li>The main navigation is at the top of the page where Moodle core shows the Home, Dashboard, My courses and Site administration navigation items already.</li><li>The menu bar is located above the main navigation, at the top of the page.</li><li>The user menu can be accessed by clicking on the user avatar in the navigation bar.</li><li>The bottom bar is placed at the bottom of the screen and can be used to implement a thumb navigation for easy access to important areas, such as the dashboard, the my courses page or the home page.</li></ul><p>Please note that upon enabling the bottom bar, the hamburger icon will be replaced by your site's logo, because users can reach the main navigation then using the bottom bar.</p>";s:28:"smartmenusmenulocationbottom";s:10:"Bottom bar";s:26:"smartmenusmenulocationmain";s:15:"Main navigation";s:26:"smartmenusmenulocationmenu";s:8:"Menu bar";s:26:"smartmenusmenulocationuser";s:9:"User menu";s:18:"smartmenusmenumode";s:9:"Menu mode";s:23:"smartmenusmenumode_help";s:358:"<p>Select the mode how the menu's items should be displayed.</p><ul><li>Submenu: The menu items is displayed as a submenu with the menu's title as parent node. This is the default option.</li><li>Inline: The menu's items are displayed directly in the navigation, one after another. Please note that this option is not supported for card type menus.</li></ul>";s:30:"smartmenusmenumoremenubehavior";s:18:"More menu behavior";s:35:"smartmenusmenumoremenubehavior_help";s:654:"<p>Select what should happen if there are too many menus to fit in the menu location.</p><ul><li>Do not change anything: No particular behaviour will be enforced, excess menus will be moved into the 'More' menu automatically.</li><li>Force into more menu: This mode moves the menu directly into the 'More' menu even if there would still be space.</li><li>Keep outside of more menu: This mode keeps the menu outside of the 'More' menu as long as possible – moving other subsequent menus to the more menu instead if needed.</li></ul><p>Please note that this setting only affects menus which are located in the main navigation or in the menu bar area.</p>";s:39:"smartmenusmenumoremenubehaviorforceinto";s:20:"Force into more menu";s:41:"smartmenusmenumoremenubehaviorkeepoutside";s:25:"Keep outside of more menu";s:30:"smartmenusmenunothingtodisplay";s:98:"There aren't any smart menus created yet. Please create your first smart menu to get things going.";s:32:"smartmenusmenupresentationheader";s:17:"Menu presentation";s:29:"smartmenusmenushowdescription";s:16:"Show description";s:34:"smartmenusmenushowdescription_help";s:491:"<p>Select if / how the description should be shown in the menu, choosing between Never, Above, Below and Help.</p><ul><li>Never: Do not show the description in the menu and use it only for internal purposes. This is the default option.</li><li>Above: Show the description at the top of the menu's list of menu items.</li><li>Below: Show the description at the end of the menu's list of menu items.</li><li>Help: Show the description as help icon near the menu's list of menu items.</li></ul>";s:34:"smartmenusmenushowdescriptionabove";s:5:"Above";s:34:"smartmenusmenushowdescriptionbelow";s:5:"Below";s:33:"smartmenusmenushowdescriptionhelp";s:4:"Help";s:34:"smartmenusmenushowdescriptionnever";s:5:"Never";s:29:"smartmenusmenustructureheader";s:14:"Menu structure";s:19:"smartmenusmenutitle";s:5:"Title";s:24:"smartmenusmenutitle_help";s:86:"The title of the menu. This will be used as the label of the parent node of this menu.";s:18:"smartmenusmenutype";s:17:"Presentation type";s:23:"smartmenusmenutype_help";s:229:"<p>Select the type of presentation for the menu, choosing between list and card.</p><ul><li>List: A list menu is composed of simple text links. This is the default option.</li><li>Card: A card menu is composed of cards.</li></ul>";s:22:"smartmenusmenutypecard";s:4:"Card";s:22:"smartmenusmenutypelist";s:4:"List";s:20:"smartmenusmodeinline";s:6:"Inline";s:21:"smartmenusmodesubmenu";s:7:"Submenu";s:20:"smartmenusnorestrict";s:14:"Not restricted";s:18:"smartmenusoperator";s:8:"Operator";s:23:"smartmenusoperator_help";s:57:"Select the operator for the cohort condition (Any or All)";s:33:"smartmenusrestrictbycohortsheader";s:30:"Restrict visibility by cohorts";s:30:"smartmenusrestrictbydateheader";s:27:"Restrict visibility by date";s:34:"smartmenusrestrictbylanguageheader";s:31:"Restrict visibility by language";s:31:"smartmenusrestrictbyrolesheader";s:28:"Restrict visibility by roles";s:31:"smartmenusrestrictbyadminheader";s:40:"Restrict visibility by site admin status";s:21:"smartmenusrolecontext";s:7:"Context";s:26:"smartmenusrolecontext_help";s:99:"Select the context for which the user's role should be checked (Any context or system context only)";s:33:"smartmenussavechangesandconfigure";s:24:"Save and configure items";s:18:"smartmenussettings";s:19:"Smart menu settings";s:15:"recommendations";s:15:"Recommendations";s:20:"recommendations_desc";s:258:"Boost Union performs just as well as the entire Moodle instance is configured. On this page, you find recommendations and checks for the optimal Boost Union operation. If you think a particular recommendation does not apply to your instance, you can mute it.";s:25:"recommendationopensetting";s:12:"Open setting";s:22:"recommendationmoreinfo";s:9:"More info";s:21:"recommendationviewall";s:24:"View all recommendations";s:21:"recommendationautofix";s:27:"Auto-fix the recommendation";s:28:"recommendationautofixsuccess";s:48:"The recommendation has been fixed automatically.";s:26:"recommendationstatusheader";s:6:"Status";s:34:"recommendationrecommendationheader";s:14:"Recommendation";s:27:"recommendationsummaryheader";s:7:"Summary";s:27:"recommendationactionsheader";s:7:"Actions";s:33:"recommendationcategory_moodlecore";s:11:"Moodle Core";s:33:"recommendationcategory_boostunion";s:11:"Boost Union";s:33:"recommendationcategory_thirdparty";s:19:"Third-party plugins";s:32:"recommendationcategory_usability";s:9:"Usability";s:36:"recommendationcategory_accessibility";s:13:"Accessibility";s:26:"recommendationcategory_mwp";s:19:"Moodle Workplace™";s:23:"recommendationstatus_ok";s:2:"OK";s:35:"recommendationstatus_ok_description";s:91:"With this recommendation, everything is perfectly fine. No action is required on your side.";s:26:"recommendationstatus_check";s:5:"Check";s:38:"recommendationstatus_check_description";s:131:"This recommendation is asking you for a manual check as Boost Union cannot automatically assess if there is really an issue or not.";s:27:"recommendationstatus_notice";s:6:"Notice";s:39:"recommendationstatus_notice_description";s:104:"This recommendation should raise your awareness, but there is no immediate need for action on your side.";s:28:"recommendationstatus_warning";s:7:"Warning";s:40:"recommendationstatus_warning_description";s:170:"This recommendation needs your attention. The recommendation's internal checks have shown that something is configured improperly and may not work as you would expect it.";s:23:"recommendationstatus_na";s:3:"N/A";s:35:"recommendationstatus_na_description";s:169:"This recommendation is not applicable to your current configuration or there is not enough data available to make a final assessment. No action is required on your side.";s:26:"recommendationstatus_muted";s:5:"Muted";s:38:"recommendationstatus_muted_description";s:125:"This recommendation is currently muted. Regardless of its original status, it will not bother you unless you unmute it again.";s:18:"recommendationmute";s:19:"Mute recommendation";s:20:"recommendationunmute";s:21:"Unmute recommendation";s:25:"recommendationmutesuccess";s:119:"The recommendation has been muted.<br />You will not be bothered by it from now on, but you can always unmute it again.";s:27:"recommendationunmutesuccess";s:36:"The recommendation has been unmuted.";s:29:"recommendationsattentionalert";s:117:"Some Boost Union recommendations need your attention. Please review the <a href="{$a->url}">Recommendations</a> page.";s:32:"recommendationsnotificationtitle";s:26:"Boost Union recommendation";s:27:"recommendationcurrentstatus";s:14:"Current status";s:31:"recommendationpossiblesolutions";s:18:"Possible solutions";s:27:"recommendationsolution_both";s:146:"You can either click the wand icon to let Boost Union auto-fix this recommendation or click the gear icon to check the affected settings yourself.";s:34:"recommendationsolution_autofixonly";s:76:"You can click the wand icon to let Boost Union auto-fix this recommendation.";s:36:"recommendationsolution_actionurlonly";s:126:"You can click the gear icon to check the affected settings, but unfortunately Boost Union cannot auto-fix this recommendation.";s:28:"recommendationsolution_check";s:197:"Please review the affected settings according to the recommendation summary. If you find that this is a false positive, you can mute this recommendation to avoid being bothered by it in the future.";s:35:"recommendation_slasharguments_title";s:23:"Slash arguments support";s:37:"recommendation_slasharguments_summary";s:86:"Slash arguments should be enabled to allow all Boost Union features to work correctly.";s:41:"recommendation_slasharguments_description";s:328:"Some Boost Union features rely on the Moodle core function slasharguments to work correctly. If slash arguments are disabled, some features of Boost Union will not work as expected, for example several flavours branding options. Please enable slash arguments in your Moodle instance to ensure the full experience of Boost Union.";s:37:"recommendation_themeboostpreset_title";s:18:"Theme Boost preset";s:39:"recommendation_themeboostpreset_summary";s:84:"The Boost preset should be set to default.scss for optimal Boost Union presentation.";s:43:"recommendation_themeboostpreset_description";s:264:"Boost Union is implemented and tested on top of the Boost preset default.scss which is the default in Moodle installations. You are free to configure a different built-in or custom Boost preset, but you should be aware that the Boost Union presentation may suffer.";s:35:"recommendation_corebrandasset_title";s:11:"{$a} upload";s:37:"recommendation_corebrandasset_summary";s:95:"A {$a} should not be uploaded in Moodle core settings as Boost Union uses its own {$a} setting.";s:41:"recommendation_corebrandasset_description";s:246:"Boost Union uses its own {$a} setting and does not use the Moodle core {$a} setting. Unless another theme is also used on this site where this {$a} will be presented, a {$a} uploaded in Moodle core is most likely never used and should be deleted.";s:41:"recommendation_coreauthinstructions_title";s:17:"Auth instructions";s:43:"recommendation_coreauthinstructions_summary";s:107:"The Moodle core authentication instructions should be empty as Boost Union uses its own login instructions.";s:47:"recommendation_coreauthinstructions_description";s:222:"Boost Union does not render Moodle core auth_instructions setting on the login page. If Boost Union is used as the theme for non-logged in users, these users will not see these instructions and thus they should be cleaned.";s:33:"recommendation_mwpextension_title";s:25:"Boost Union MWP extension";s:35:"recommendation_mwpextension_summary";s:86:"The Boost Union MWP extension should be installed when running on Moodle Workplace™.";s:39:"recommendation_mwpextension_description";s:661:"Boost Union has detected that this Moodle instance is running on Moodle Workplace™ as the tool_tenant plugin is installed. However, the Boost Union MWP extension is not installed. Without this extension, Boost Union but will lack essential Moodle Workplace™ widgets and won't have any support for tenants.<br /><br />But don't worry, there is the Boost Union MWP edition which provides full Moodle Workplace™ support and which is maintained by Boost Union co-maintainer bdecent. If you want to use Boost Union on Moodle Workplace™, you can find all details on the <a href="https://bdecent.de/union" target="_blank">bdecent product presentation page</a>.";s:16:"privacy:metadata";s:70:"The Boost Union theme does not store any personal data about any user.";s:21:"boost_union:configure";s:46:"To be able to configure the theme as non-admin";s:36:"boost_union:viewhintcourseguestenrol";s:65:"To be able to see a hint for guest enrolment in a visible course.";s:35:"boost_union:viewhintcourseselfenrol";s:77:"To be able to see a hint for unrestricted self enrolment in a visible course.";s:34:"boost_union:viewhintinhiddencourse";s:44:"To be able to see a hint in a hidden course.";s:28:"boost_union:viewregionheader";s:41:"To be able to see the Header block region";s:28:"boost_union:editregionheader";s:42:"To be able to edit the Header block region";s:33:"boost_union:viewregionoutsideleft";s:49:"To be able to see the Outside (left) block region";s:33:"boost_union:editregionoutsideleft";s:50:"To be able to edit the Outside (left) block region";s:34:"boost_union:viewregionoutsideright";s:50:"To be able to see the Outside (right) block region";s:34:"boost_union:editregionoutsideright";s:51:"To be able to edit the Outside (right) block region";s:32:"boost_union:viewregionoutsidetop";s:48:"To be able to see the Outside (top) block region";s:32:"boost_union:editregionoutsidetop";s:49:"To be able to edit the Outside (top) block region";s:35:"boost_union:viewregionoutsidebottom";s:51:"To be able to see the Outside (bottom) block region";s:35:"boost_union:editregionoutsidebottom";s:52:"To be able to edit the Outside (bottom) block region";s:34:"boost_union:viewregioncontentupper";s:50:"To be able to see the Content (upper) block region";s:34:"boost_union:editregioncontentupper";s:51:"To be able to edit the Content (upper) block region";s:34:"boost_union:viewregioncontentlower";s:50:"To be able to see the Content (lower) block region";s:34:"boost_union:editregioncontentlower";s:51:"To be able to edit the Content (lower) block region";s:32:"boost_union:viewregionfooterleft";s:48:"To be able to see the Footer (left) block region";s:32:"boost_union:editregionfooterleft";s:49:"To be able to edit the Footer (left) block region";s:33:"boost_union:viewregionfooterright";s:49:"To be able to see the Footer (right) block region";s:33:"boost_union:editregionfooterright";s:50:"To be able to edit the Footer (right) block region";s:34:"boost_union:viewregionfootercenter";s:50:"To be able to see the Footer (center) block region";s:34:"boost_union:editregionfootercenter";s:51:"To be able to edit the Footer (center) block region";s:35:"boost_union:viewregionoffcanvasleft";s:52:"To be able to see the Off-canvas (left) block region";s:35:"boost_union:editregionoffcanvasleft";s:53:"To be able to edit the Off-canvas (left) block region";s:36:"boost_union:viewregionoffcanvasright";s:53:"To be able to see the Off-canvas (right) block region";s:36:"boost_union:editregionoffcanvasright";s:54:"To be able to edit the Off-canvas (right) block region";s:37:"boost_union:viewregionoffcanvascenter";s:54:"To be able to see the Off-canvas (center) block region";s:37:"boost_union:editregionoffcanvascenter";s:55:"To be able to edit the Off-canvas (center) block region";s:17:"cachedef_flavours";s:71:"Flavours which apply to a given page's category ID for the current user";s:19:"cachedef_smartmenus";s:11:"Smart menus";s:24:"cachedef_smartmenu_items";s:16:"Smart menu items";s:22:"cachedef_touchiconsios";s:24:"Touch icon files for iOS";s:21:"cachedef_hooksuppress";s:17:"Hook suppressions";s:25:"cachedef_fontawesomeicons";s:20:"FontAwesome icon map";s:15:"task_purgecache";s:17:"Purge theme cache";s:20:"checkrecommendations";s:27:"Boost Union recommendations";s:22:"checkrecommendationsok";s:56:"No Boost Union recommendations currently need attention.";s:27:"checkrecommendationswarning";s:56:"At least one Boost Union recommendation needs attention.";s:27:"checkrecommendationsdetails";s:75:"Review recommendations on the <a href="{$a->url}">Recommendations</a> page.";s:24:"upgradenotice_2022080922";s:144:"From this release on, Boost Union has its own logo and compact logo settings and does not use these files from the Moodle core settings anymore.";s:29:"upgradenotice_2022080922_logo";s:4:"logo";s:36:"upgradenotice_2022080922_logocompact";s:12:"compact logo";s:31:"upgradenotice_2022080922_copied";s:165:"The existing <strong>{$a}</strong> from the Moodle core settings has been copied to the Boost Union {$a} setting during this upgrade. Please double-check the result.";s:34:"upgradenotice_2022080922_notcopied";s:180:"The <strong>{$a}</strong> setting within Boost Union is empty now. If you want to use a {$a} within Boost Union from now on, just upload it into the Boost Union {$a} setting later.";s:24:"upgradenotice_2025041410";s:223:"The setting "Show hint for guest access" has been updated to support more options. Your existing configuration (which was set to "Yes") has been migrated to the new option "Yes, but only if no guest access password is set".";s:24:"upgradenotice_2025041413";s:168:"The setting "courselistinghowfields" has been renamed to "courselistingshowfields" to fix a typo. Your existing configuration has been migrated to the new setting name.";s:24:"upgradenotice_2025041416";s:190:"Smart menu dividers are now available as a dedicated menu item type. Existing dividers (created using heading type with hash signs) have been automatically converted to the new divider type.";s:24:"upgradenotice_2025100623";s:418:"The navbar color options "Primary color navbar with dark font color" and "Primary color navbar with light font color" have been renamed to "Colored navbar with dark font color" and "Colored navbar with light font color". Your existing configuration has been migrated automatically. Additionally, your primary brand color has been transferred to the new "Navbar tint" setting to maintain the previous visual appearance.";}